INSERT INTO sat_questions (question_id, external_id, vault_id, disclosed_item_id, source, program, test_type, test_type_desc, domain, primary_class_cd, skill_cd, skill_desc, difficulty, score_band_range_cd, question_type, stimulus_html, stem_html, answer_options, correct_answer, answer_keys, rationale_html, correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale, image_count, parent_template_name, parent_template_id, template_cluster_id, template_cluster_name, origin, position, answer_style, section, raw_payload, created_date, updated_date) VALUES
    ($SATQ$aaa3ee7c$SATQ$, $SATQ$e1c2edb3-9696-4ebc-97eb-0f9439d30a41$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$715aad5d-b8ba-4e5f-a4b6-86e7cdde7539$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Critics have asserted that fine art and fashion rarely <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> in a world where artists create timeless works for exhibition and designers periodically produce new styles for the public to buy. Luise&ntilde;o/Shoshone-Bannock beadwork artist and designer Jamie Okuma challenges this view: her work can be seen in the Metropolitan Museum of Art and purchased through her online boutique.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"8db5c3c2-ca17-485f-8742-9ed6260c403b","content":"<p>prevail</p>"},{"id":"a04e3215-9c0a-4199-8cf8-a663277298e1","content":"<p>succumb</p>"},{"id":"385d6b99-575a-4f42-9ce4-7a05c606dcdd","content":"<p>diverge</p>"},{"id":"ac7ec7ca-ce19-4d03-ab5a-73548d9d140e","content":"<p>intersect</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ac7ec7ca-ce19-4d03-ab5a-73548d9d140e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion about the relationship between fine art and fashion. As used in this context, &ldquo;intersect&rdquo; means to connect or overlap. The text indicates that Jamie Okuma challenges the position held by critics because her work can be seen at an art museum and can be bought by the public from her online boutique. The text also presents the critics&rsquo; view as being influenced by a perception that fine artists create works that are &ldquo;timeless&rdquo; and meant for exhibition, whereas fashion designers periodically produce new styles that are meant for purchase. This context suggests that the critics believe that fine art and fashion tend not to overlap&mdash;in other words, that they rarely intersect.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to say that critics contend that fine art and fashion rarely &ldquo;prevail,&rdquo; or prove to be triumphant or widespread. The text indicates that Okuma is an example of an artist who demonstrates that it&rsquo;s possible to make fine art that is also available to the public as fashion. Choice B is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to say that fine art and fashion rarely &ldquo;succumb,&rdquo; or surrender. The text establishes that unlike what critics believe, Okuma creates works that are in art museums and available for the public to purchase, suggesting that critics believe fine art and fashion rarely overlap, not that they rarely succumb. Choice C is incorrect because saying that critics believe that fine art and fashion rarely &ldquo;diverge,&rdquo; or disagree or move in different directions, wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context. The text presents Okuma&rsquo;s work as both fine art and fashion, thereby undermining what the critics assert. This suggests that the critics believe that fine art and fashion rarely intersect rather than that the two rarely diverge. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-941-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$988aa92d-c517-487c-bac2-b2c5a1541998$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"aaa3ee7c","external_id":"e1c2edb3-9696-4ebc-97eb-0f9439d30a41","vaultid":"715aad5d-b8ba-4e5f-a4b6-86e7cdde7539","uId":"679af193-471a-440a-af94-c3a6955e1f23","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Critics have asserted that fine art and fashion rarely <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> in a world where artists create timeless works for exhibition and designers periodically produce new styles for the public to buy. Luise&ntilde;o/Shoshone-Bannock beadwork artist and designer Jamie Okuma challenges this view: her work can be seen in the Metropolitan Museum of Art and purchased through her online boutique.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8db5c3c2-ca17-485f-8742-9ed6260c403b","content":"<p>prevail</p>"},{"id":"a04e3215-9c0a-4199-8cf8-a663277298e1","content":"<p>succumb</p>"},{"id":"385d6b99-575a-4f42-9ce4-7a05c606dcdd","content":"<p>diverge</p>"},{"id":"ac7ec7ca-ce19-4d03-ab5a-73548d9d140e","content":"<p>intersect</p>"}],"keys":["ac7ec7ca-ce19-4d03-ab5a-73548d9d140e"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion about the relationship between fine art and fashion. As used in this context, &ldquo;intersect&rdquo; means to connect or overlap. The text indicates that Jamie Okuma challenges the position held by critics because her work can be seen at an art museum and can be bought by the public from her online boutique. The text also presents the critics&rsquo; view as being influenced by a perception that fine artists create works that are &ldquo;timeless&rdquo; and meant for exhibition, whereas fashion designers periodically produce new styles that are meant for purchase. This context suggests that the critics believe that fine art and fashion tend not to overlap&mdash;in other words, that they rarely intersect.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to say that critics contend that fine art and fashion rarely &ldquo;prevail,&rdquo; or prove to be triumphant or widespread. The text indicates that Okuma is an example of an artist who demonstrates that it&rsquo;s possible to make fine art that is also available to the public as fashion. Choice B is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to say that fine art and fashion rarely &ldquo;succumb,&rdquo; or surrender. The text establishes that unlike what critics believe, Okuma creates works that are in art museums and available for the public to purchase, suggesting that critics believe fine art and fashion rarely overlap, not that they rarely succumb. Choice C is incorrect because saying that critics believe that fine art and fashion rarely &ldquo;diverge,&rdquo; or disagree or move in different directions, wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context. The text presents Okuma&rsquo;s work as both fine art and fashion, thereby undermining what the critics assert. This suggests that the critics believe that fine art and fashion rarely intersect rather than that the two rarely diverge. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-941-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"988aa92d-c517-487c-bac2-b2c5a1541998","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959356,"updateDate":1691007959356}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959356, 1691007959356),
    ($SATQ$aad56f2b$SATQ$, $SATQ$ffd55ab0-aa98-4695-aab9-4c91355810ed$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$6133a01e-35ef-4b43-9509-a50bcc271dcc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As a young photographer in the 1950s, William Klein <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> the conventions of photography by creating images that were high contrast and included blurred and distorted elements&mdash;features generally seen as flaws. So unorthodox was Klein&rsquo;s work that he had difficulty finding a publisher for his now-iconic 1956 photo book <em>Life is Good &amp; Good for You in New York</em>.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3f403ed1-1aa9-4103-bbe0-95b61bdb75ae","content":"<p>reviewed</p>"},{"id":"c1d9e935-e567-4a5e-9458-ae59ce1ed74c","content":"<p>defied</p>"},{"id":"099bf3d4-3223-4d49-929b-4a940379a1d6","content":"<p>respected</p>"},{"id":"ce7e58e8-d06a-4e15-b254-1aa2ce0f50e1","content":"<p>prevented</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c1d9e935-e567-4a5e-9458-ae59ce1ed74c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. "Defied" means "resisted" or "deliberately disobeyed," which matches the way Klein broke from the conventions of photography in his time by including features that were generally seen as flaws.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. "Reviewed" means "analyzed" or "evaluated," but that doesn&rsquo;t really fit the context here. Klein isn&rsquo;t directly providing any thoughtful examination of the conventions of photography: he&rsquo;s just breaking all the rules. Choice C is incorrect. "Respected" can mean "admired" or "followed" (as in the case of conventions). It&rsquo;s clear that Klein didn&rsquo;t respect conventions, given his use of photographic features that were generally considered "flaws." Choice D is incorrect. "Prevented" means "stopped," and Klein did not stop the conventions&mdash;they still existed. Instead, he made images that were seen as "flawed" under those conventions.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-WIC-M006$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$53dfc88d-625b-4cf4-8694-d0c26bb9377b$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"aad56f2b","external_id":"ffd55ab0-aa98-4695-aab9-4c91355810ed","vaultid":"6133a01e-35ef-4b43-9509-a50bcc271dcc","uId":"dc90186c-5c41-412f-8911-d257fd757f34","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>As a young photographer in the 1950s, William Klein <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> the conventions of photography by creating images that were high contrast and included blurred and distorted elements&mdash;features generally seen as flaws. So unorthodox was Klein&rsquo;s work that he had difficulty finding a publisher for his now-iconic 1956 photo book <em>Life is Good &amp; Good for You in New York</em>.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3f403ed1-1aa9-4103-bbe0-95b61bdb75ae","content":"<p>reviewed</p>"},{"id":"c1d9e935-e567-4a5e-9458-ae59ce1ed74c","content":"<p>defied</p>"},{"id":"099bf3d4-3223-4d49-929b-4a940379a1d6","content":"<p>respected</p>"},{"id":"ce7e58e8-d06a-4e15-b254-1aa2ce0f50e1","content":"<p>prevented</p>"}],"keys":["c1d9e935-e567-4a5e-9458-ae59ce1ed74c"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. \"Defied\" means \"resisted\" or \"deliberately disobeyed,\" which matches the way Klein broke from the conventions of photography in his time by including features that were generally seen as flaws.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. \"Reviewed\" means \"analyzed\" or \"evaluated,\" but that doesn&rsquo;t really fit the context here. Klein isn&rsquo;t directly providing any thoughtful examination of the conventions of photography: he&rsquo;s just breaking all the rules. Choice C is incorrect. \"Respected\" can mean \"admired\" or \"followed\" (as in the case of conventions). It&rsquo;s clear that Klein didn&rsquo;t respect conventions, given his use of photographic features that were generally considered \"flaws.\" Choice D is incorrect. \"Prevented\" means \"stopped,\" and Klein did not stop the conventions&mdash;they still existed. Instead, he made images that were seen as \"flawed\" under those conventions.</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-WIC-M006","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"53dfc88d-625b-4cf4-8694-d0c26bb9377b","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959378,"updateDate":1691007959378}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959378, 1691007959378),
    ($SATQ$ab1bd603$SATQ$, $SATQ$70b8fe32-ad91-4e0a-9e70-fc607d6bda0d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is adapted from Upton Sinclair&rsquo;s 1906 novel&nbsp;<em>The Jungle</em>. Marija is helping to manage her sister&rsquo;s wedding.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It was [Marija&rsquo;s] task to see that all things went in due form, and after the best home traditions; and, flying wildly hither and thither, bowling every one out of the way, and scolding and exhorting all day with her tremendous voice, Marija was too eager to see that others conformed to the proprieties to <span style="text-decoration: underline;" role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">consider</span><em> </em>them herself.</p>
</blockquote>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;consider&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b56fd996-a628-4889-b4c5-0ab4eb4bdb32","content":"<p>Take into account and follow</p>"},{"id":"ce1d24a4-f507-4f89-9fdf-069fa49fa935","content":"<p>Admire steadily and praise</p>"},{"id":"c9087a44-ff04-4e77-bdec-b2a72f60b812","content":"<p>Come to a decision about</p>"},{"id":"7993b392-da49-44e3-9895-a747b231b8d7","content":"<p>Have an opinion on</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["b56fd996-a628-4889-b4c5-0ab4eb4bdb32"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because as used in the text, "consider" most nearly means to take into account and follow. The text explains that Marija&rsquo;s job was to make sure that her sister&rsquo;s wedding proceeded in certain ways ("in due form") and that she loudly directed everyone&rsquo;s actions all day. The text then indicates that Marija was so focused on ensuring that others "conformed to the proprieties"&mdash;that is, that they behaved in appropriate ways&mdash;that she failed to "consider them herself"; that is, she didn&rsquo;t take standards of appropriate behavior into account and follow them in her own actions.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. In some contexts, "consider" can mean to think about something in a positive way&mdash;which can involve admiration&mdash;but the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Marija was so busy imposing "proprieties" (standards of appropriate behavior) on others that she didn&rsquo;t admire and praise them herself. The context suggests it&rsquo;s more likely that Marija did speak positively of "due form" and "the best home traditions" while ensuring others behaved in certain ways. Choice C is incorrect. In some contexts, "consider" can mean to come to a decision, but the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Marija wasn&rsquo;t able to make a decision for herself about the "proprieties" (standards of appropriate behavior) she ensured everyone else conformed to. Rather, the context conveys that Marija knew very clearly which behaviors others should follow as "due form" and "the best home traditions." Choice D is incorrect. In some contexts, "consider" can mean to have an opinion, but the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Marija wasn&rsquo;t able to have an opinion on the "proprieties" (standards of appropriate behavior) she was ensuring others conformed to. Rather, the context conveys that Marija had strong feelings about which behaviors were "due form" and "the best home traditions."</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ab1bd603","external_id":"70b8fe32-ad91-4e0a-9e70-fc607d6bda0d","vaultid":null,"uId":"5645d8ba-cac1-4922-ac1d-42c601a08aaf","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is adapted from Upton Sinclair&rsquo;s 1906 novel&nbsp;<em>The Jungle</em>. Marija is helping to manage her sister&rsquo;s wedding.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It was [Marija&rsquo;s] task to see that all things went in due form, and after the best home traditions; and, flying wildly hither and thither, bowling every one out of the way, and scolding and exhorting all day with her tremendous voice, Marija was too eager to see that others conformed to the proprieties to <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">consider</span><em> </em>them herself.</p>\n</blockquote>","stem":"<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;consider&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b56fd996-a628-4889-b4c5-0ab4eb4bdb32","content":"<p>Take into account and follow</p>"},{"id":"ce1d24a4-f507-4f89-9fdf-069fa49fa935","content":"<p>Admire steadily and praise</p>"},{"id":"c9087a44-ff04-4e77-bdec-b2a72f60b812","content":"<p>Come to a decision about</p>"},{"id":"7993b392-da49-44e3-9895-a747b231b8d7","content":"<p>Have an opinion on</p>"}],"keys":["b56fd996-a628-4889-b4c5-0ab4eb4bdb32"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because as used in the text, \"consider\" most nearly means to take into account and follow. The text explains that Marija&rsquo;s job was to make sure that her sister&rsquo;s wedding proceeded in certain ways (\"in due form\") and that she loudly directed everyone&rsquo;s actions all day. The text then indicates that Marija was so focused on ensuring that others \"conformed to the proprieties\"&mdash;that is, that they behaved in appropriate ways&mdash;that she failed to \"consider them herself\"; that is, she didn&rsquo;t take standards of appropriate behavior into account and follow them in her own actions.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. In some contexts, \"consider\" can mean to think about something in a positive way&mdash;which can involve admiration&mdash;but the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Marija was so busy imposing \"proprieties\" (standards of appropriate behavior) on others that she didn&rsquo;t admire and praise them herself. The context suggests it&rsquo;s more likely that Marija did speak positively of \"due form\" and \"the best home traditions\" while ensuring others behaved in certain ways. Choice C is incorrect. In some contexts, \"consider\" can mean to come to a decision, but the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Marija wasn&rsquo;t able to make a decision for herself about the \"proprieties\" (standards of appropriate behavior) she ensured everyone else conformed to. Rather, the context conveys that Marija knew very clearly which behaviors others should follow as \"due form\" and \"the best home traditions.\" Choice D is incorrect. In some contexts, \"consider\" can mean to have an opinion, but the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Marija wasn&rsquo;t able to have an opinion on the \"proprieties\" (standards of appropriate behavior) she was ensuring others conformed to. Rather, the context conveys that Marija had strong feelings about which behaviors were \"due form\" and \"the best home traditions.\"</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061178,"updateDate":1755117061178}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061178, 1755117061178),
    ($SATQ$ab56a107$SATQ$, $SATQ$6ea6be63-d92d-4ba8-8655-262858f55e62$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$0aa2c4d8-dffc-4980-af72-559ea69184dc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Cross-Text Connections$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>&nbsp;</p><p><span aria-level="2" role="heading"><strong>Text 1</strong></span></p>
<p>Digital art, the use of digital technology to create or display images, isn&rsquo;t really art at all. It doesn&rsquo;t require as much skill as creating physical art. &ldquo;Painting&rdquo; with a tablet and stylus is much easier than using paint and a brush: the technology is doing most of the work.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p><p><span aria-level="2" role="heading"><strong>Text 2</strong></span></p>
<p>The painting programs used to create digital art involve more than just pressing a few buttons. In addition to knowing the fundamentals of art, digital artists need to be familiar with sophisticated software. Many artists will start by drawing an image on paper before transforming the piece to a digital format, where they can apply a variety of colors and techniques that would otherwise require many different traditional tools. </p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claims of the author of Text 1?&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f0076977-6e11-445f-909d-a32a60e7ce96","content":"<p>By arguing that a piece of art created digitally can still be displayed traditionally</p>"},{"id":"853fcaa7-91b1-410d-a361-000cb3d24016","content":"<p>By explaining that it&rsquo;s actually much harder to use a tablet and stylus to create art than to use paint and a brush</p>"},{"id":"05f1ba00-9134-4e9a-9741-f6cc6f12864f","content":"<p>By insisting that digital art requires artistic abilities and skill even if it employs less traditional tools</p>"},{"id":"d0833b56-143d-4c7d-847d-99318cff37ee","content":"<p>By admitting that most digital artists don&rsquo;t think fundamental drawing skills are important</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["05f1ba00-9134-4e9a-9741-f6cc6f12864f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it reflects how the author of Text 2 would respond to the claims in Text 1. Both texts address skills needed to produce digital art. Text 1 claims that digital art doesn&rsquo;t require the same amount of skill as creating physical art and that &ldquo;the technology is doing most of the work.&rdquo; Text 2 states that digital art requires &ldquo;knowing the fundamentals of art&rdquo; and that many digital artists begin their work on paper and then transfer it to a digital format using &ldquo;sophisticated software&rdquo; and &ldquo;a variety of colors and techniques.&rdquo; Therefore, the author of Text 2 would most likely insist that digital art requires artistic abilities even if it employs less traditional tools. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because neither text discusses nondigital means of displaying art. Choice B is incorrect because the author of Text 2 doesn&rsquo;t address whether it&rsquo;s harder to use a tablet and stylus than it is to use paint and a brush. Text 2 does argue that digital art requires skills that aren&rsquo;t part of the traditional methods for producing art, but the text doesn&rsquo;t address relative difficulty. Choice D is incorrect because the author of Text 2 states that digital artists still need to know &ldquo;the fundamentals of art&rdquo; and that many digital artists begin their work by drafting on paper before transferring the work to a digital format. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-012-CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$ad04f83d-0100-44aa-928a-fc6934c95bf5$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ab56a107","external_id":"6ea6be63-d92d-4ba8-8655-262858f55e62","vaultid":"0aa2c4d8-dffc-4980-af72-559ea69184dc","uId":"c289656d-e40b-468f-81c4-04bbb574c601","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"CTC","skill_desc":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>&nbsp;</p><p><span aria-level=\"2\" role=\"heading\"><strong>Text 1</strong></span></p>\n<p>Digital art, the use of digital technology to create or display images, isn&rsquo;t really art at all. It doesn&rsquo;t require as much skill as creating physical art. &ldquo;Painting&rdquo; with a tablet and stylus is much easier than using paint and a brush: the technology is doing most of the work.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p><p><span aria-level=\"2\" role=\"heading\"><strong>Text 2</strong></span></p>\n<p>The painting programs used to create digital art involve more than just pressing a few buttons. In addition to knowing the fundamentals of art, digital artists need to be familiar with sophisticated software. Many artists will start by drawing an image on paper before transforming the piece to a digital format, where they can apply a variety of colors and techniques that would otherwise require many different traditional tools. </p>","stem":"<p>Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claims of the author of Text 1?&nbsp;</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f0076977-6e11-445f-909d-a32a60e7ce96","content":"<p>By arguing that a piece of art created digitally can still be displayed traditionally</p>"},{"id":"853fcaa7-91b1-410d-a361-000cb3d24016","content":"<p>By explaining that it&rsquo;s actually much harder to use a tablet and stylus to create art than to use paint and a brush</p>"},{"id":"05f1ba00-9134-4e9a-9741-f6cc6f12864f","content":"<p>By insisting that digital art requires artistic abilities and skill even if it employs less traditional tools</p>"},{"id":"d0833b56-143d-4c7d-847d-99318cff37ee","content":"<p>By admitting that most digital artists don&rsquo;t think fundamental drawing skills are important</p>"}],"keys":["05f1ba00-9134-4e9a-9741-f6cc6f12864f"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it reflects how the author of Text 2 would respond to the claims in Text 1. Both texts address skills needed to produce digital art. Text 1 claims that digital art doesn&rsquo;t require the same amount of skill as creating physical art and that &ldquo;the technology is doing most of the work.&rdquo; Text 2 states that digital art requires &ldquo;knowing the fundamentals of art&rdquo; and that many digital artists begin their work on paper and then transfer it to a digital format using &ldquo;sophisticated software&rdquo; and &ldquo;a variety of colors and techniques.&rdquo; Therefore, the author of Text 2 would most likely insist that digital art requires artistic abilities even if it employs less traditional tools. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because neither text discusses nondigital means of displaying art. Choice B is incorrect because the author of Text 2 doesn&rsquo;t address whether it&rsquo;s harder to use a tablet and stylus than it is to use paint and a brush. Text 2 does argue that digital art requires skills that aren&rsquo;t part of the traditional methods for producing art, but the text doesn&rsquo;t address relative difficulty. Choice D is incorrect because the author of Text 2 states that digital artists still need to know &ldquo;the fundamentals of art&rdquo; and that many digital artists begin their work by drafting on paper before transferring the work to a digital format. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-012-CTC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"ad04f83d-0100-44aa-928a-fc6934c95bf5","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959314,"updateDate":1691007959314}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959314, 1691007959314),
    ($SATQ$ac5bf490$SATQ$, $SATQ$a7ad458a-f29f-46e2-9e97-afc78847295d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from Reyna Grande&rsquo;s 2012 memoir <em>The Distance Between Us</em>. In the text, Grande reflects on a time when she and her older sister Mago were children. A Barbie is a type of doll.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I begged Mago to come play with me. She wasn&rsquo;t as interested in my Barbie as she had been just two months before, <span style="text-decoration: underline;" role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">which made me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for</span>. Usually, it was me doing the envying. After I pestered her relentlessly, she finally put her notebook down and came over to me.</p>
</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: right;"><span class="dap_copyright">&copy;2012 by Reyna Grande</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1406f83f-fc53-44b9-8986-1742e7747316","content":"<p>It indicates Grande&rsquo;s unhappiness over Mago&rsquo;s disinterest in Grande&rsquo;s doll.</p>"},{"id":"f2a7ac6b-5f16-4506-9b0b-708ec3777d7e","content":"<p>It expresses Grande&rsquo;s anger over Mago&rsquo;s refusal to spend time with her.</p>"},{"id":"49bb5781-7107-411b-ae61-16d25bc8a959","content":"<p>It presents an example of how Mago and Grande generally played together as children.</p>"},{"id":"ced0c9a9-b64b-4c4d-ae64-2fdb0bd25b91","content":"<p>It provides a reason for why Mago is unwilling to play with Grande.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1406f83f-fc53-44b9-8986-1742e7747316"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes the function of the underlined portion in the text. The underlined portion ("which made me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for") directly expresses Grande&rsquo;s unhappiness about her sister&rsquo;s diminished interest in her Barbie doll. The underlined text specifically identifies that Grande feels sad and explains why Mago&rsquo;s disinterest particularly affects her&mdash;because it was the one rare instance where her older sister had envied her, rather than the reverse.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the underlined portion expresses sadness, not anger. Although there is some correspondence between the emotions anger and envy and the text does indicate that Grande usually envies her sister, the underlined portion states that Grande feels sad about Mago&rsquo;s disinterest in Grande&rsquo;s Barbie, not angry about Mago&rsquo;s refusal to spend time with her. Choice C is incorrect. While the first part of the sentence that contains the underlined portion indicates that Mago has previously taken an interest in Grande&rsquo;s Barbie, implying that the sisters may regularly have played with the Barbie together in the past, the underlined portion doesn&rsquo;t provide an example of this. The underlined portion instead explains why Mago&rsquo;s recently developed disinterest in the Barbie saddens Grande. Choice D is incorrect because neither the underlined portion nor the text as a whole explains why Mago is unwilling to play with Grande. Rather than addressing Mago&rsquo;s motivation or reasoning, the underlined portion describes Grande&rsquo;s emotional reaction to Mago&rsquo;s disinterest in Grande&rsquo;s Barbie and explains why this lack of interest matters to Grande.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ac5bf490","external_id":"a7ad458a-f29f-46e2-9e97-afc78847295d","vaultid":null,"uId":"a1a1c45f-ecb0-4123-bbf0-c76f9f4b3866","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from Reyna Grande&rsquo;s 2012 memoir <em>The Distance Between Us</em>. In the text, Grande reflects on a time when she and her older sister Mago were children. A Barbie is a type of doll.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I begged Mago to come play with me. She wasn&rsquo;t as interested in my Barbie as she had been just two months before, <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">which made me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for</span>. Usually, it was me doing the envying. After I pestered her relentlessly, she finally put her notebook down and came over to me.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p style=\"text-align: right;\"><span class=\"dap_copyright\">&copy;2012 by Reyna Grande</span></p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1406f83f-fc53-44b9-8986-1742e7747316","content":"<p>It indicates Grande&rsquo;s unhappiness over Mago&rsquo;s disinterest in Grande&rsquo;s doll.</p>"},{"id":"f2a7ac6b-5f16-4506-9b0b-708ec3777d7e","content":"<p>It expresses Grande&rsquo;s anger over Mago&rsquo;s refusal to spend time with her.</p>"},{"id":"49bb5781-7107-411b-ae61-16d25bc8a959","content":"<p>It presents an example of how Mago and Grande generally played together as children.</p>"},{"id":"ced0c9a9-b64b-4c4d-ae64-2fdb0bd25b91","content":"<p>It provides a reason for why Mago is unwilling to play with Grande.</p>"}],"keys":["1406f83f-fc53-44b9-8986-1742e7747316"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes the function of the underlined portion in the text. The underlined portion (\"which made me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for\") directly expresses Grande&rsquo;s unhappiness about her sister&rsquo;s diminished interest in her Barbie doll. The underlined text specifically identifies that Grande feels sad and explains why Mago&rsquo;s disinterest particularly affects her&mdash;because it was the one rare instance where her older sister had envied her, rather than the reverse.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the underlined portion expresses sadness, not anger. Although there is some correspondence between the emotions anger and envy and the text does indicate that Grande usually envies her sister, the underlined portion states that Grande feels sad about Mago&rsquo;s disinterest in Grande&rsquo;s Barbie, not angry about Mago&rsquo;s refusal to spend time with her. Choice C is incorrect. While the first part of the sentence that contains the underlined portion indicates that Mago has previously taken an interest in Grande&rsquo;s Barbie, implying that the sisters may regularly have played with the Barbie together in the past, the underlined portion doesn&rsquo;t provide an example of this. The underlined portion instead explains why Mago&rsquo;s recently developed disinterest in the Barbie saddens Grande. Choice D is incorrect because neither the underlined portion nor the text as a whole explains why Mago is unwilling to play with Grande. Rather than addressing Mago&rsquo;s motivation or reasoning, the underlined portion describes Grande&rsquo;s emotional reaction to Mago&rsquo;s disinterest in Grande&rsquo;s Barbie and explains why this lack of interest matters to Grande.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061190,"updateDate":1755117061190}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061190, 1755117061190),
    ($SATQ$ac9a3a26$SATQ$, $SATQ$f00cced1-627e-44ea-8df1-1426316e7a88$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$64a5682d-964b-4949-957c-f2af4cb017df$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>According to historian Vicki L. Ruiz, Mexican American women made crucial contributions to the labor movement during World War II. At the time, food processing companies entered into contracts to supply United States armed forces with canned goods. Increased production quotas conferred greater bargaining power on the companies&rsquo; employees, many of whom were Mexican American women: <span role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content"><u>employees insisted on more favorable benefits, and employers, who were anxious to fulfill the contracts, complied.</u></span> Thus, labor activism became a platform for Mexican American women to assert their agency.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"572a4eb5-2379-4487-89e4-3a4b18455990","content":"<p>It elaborates on a claim about labor relations in a particular industry made earlier in the text.</p>"},{"id":"b7d8a6d8-4bb1-491f-b1b9-2bb1dae7f8b3","content":"<p>It offers an example of a trend in the World War II&ndash;era economy discussed earlier in the text.</p>"},{"id":"8574440b-2f73-4a11-a9de-9c939fe2594f","content":"<p>It notes a possible exception to the historical narrative of labor activism sketched earlier in the text.</p>"},{"id":"9372fc55-bf4c-4766-9d99-af8aea64d6e3","content":"<p>It provides further details about the identities of the workers discussed earlier in the text.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["572a4eb5-2379-4487-89e4-3a4b18455990"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it best describes how the underlined portion functions in the text as a whole. The text says that the increased production quotas of food processing companies during World War II enabled employees to make better bargains in exchange for their labor. The underlined portion presents an example of this increased bargaining power: employees requested more favorable benefits, and employers complied because they were under pressure to fulfill the demanding terms of their contracts. Thus, the underlined portion of the text elaborates on a claim about labor relations in a particular industry (food processing) made earlier in the text. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because there is no indication in the text that the economic factors that influenced food processing also influenced other parts of the economy; thus, the bargaining described in the underlined portion of the text cannot be called an example of a trend. Choice C is incorrect because the underlined portion supports the historical narrative of labor activism in food processing that is sketched in the text, instead of noting an exception to that narrative. Choice D is incorrect because while the underlined portion does discuss the demands that workers made in exchange for their labor, it does not discuss the identities of the workers. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-009-TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$24a4032f-b446-43fd-b2ad-70d28ff832c4$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ac9a3a26","external_id":"f00cced1-627e-44ea-8df1-1426316e7a88","vaultid":"64a5682d-964b-4949-957c-f2af4cb017df","uId":"1dddd092-c772-4d86-abfa-44d31120ec46","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>According to historian Vicki L. Ruiz, Mexican American women made crucial contributions to the labor movement during World War II. At the time, food processing companies entered into contracts to supply United States armed forces with canned goods. Increased production quotas conferred greater bargaining power on the companies&rsquo; employees, many of whom were Mexican American women: <span role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\"><u>employees insisted on more favorable benefits, and employers, who were anxious to fulfill the contracts, complied.</u></span> Thus, labor activism became a platform for Mexican American women to assert their agency.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"572a4eb5-2379-4487-89e4-3a4b18455990","content":"<p>It elaborates on a claim about labor relations in a particular industry made earlier in the text.</p>"},{"id":"b7d8a6d8-4bb1-491f-b1b9-2bb1dae7f8b3","content":"<p>It offers an example of a trend in the World War II&ndash;era economy discussed earlier in the text.</p>"},{"id":"8574440b-2f73-4a11-a9de-9c939fe2594f","content":"<p>It notes a possible exception to the historical narrative of labor activism sketched earlier in the text.</p>"},{"id":"9372fc55-bf4c-4766-9d99-af8aea64d6e3","content":"<p>It provides further details about the identities of the workers discussed earlier in the text.</p>"}],"keys":["572a4eb5-2379-4487-89e4-3a4b18455990"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it best describes how the underlined portion functions in the text as a whole. The text says that the increased production quotas of food processing companies during World War II enabled employees to make better bargains in exchange for their labor. The underlined portion presents an example of this increased bargaining power: employees requested more favorable benefits, and employers complied because they were under pressure to fulfill the demanding terms of their contracts. Thus, the underlined portion of the text elaborates on a claim about labor relations in a particular industry (food processing) made earlier in the text. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because there is no indication in the text that the economic factors that influenced food processing also influenced other parts of the economy; thus, the bargaining described in the underlined portion of the text cannot be called an example of a trend. Choice C is incorrect because the underlined portion supports the historical narrative of labor activism in food processing that is sketched in the text, instead of noting an exception to that narrative. Choice D is incorrect because while the underlined portion does discuss the demands that workers made in exchange for their labor, it does not discuss the identities of the workers. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-009-TSP","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"24a4032f-b446-43fd-b2ad-70d28ff832c4","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959314,"updateDate":1691007959314}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959314, 1691007959314),
    ($SATQ$acb852e7$SATQ$, $SATQ$5f5ee9b3-7025-41ae-ac00-71afc199772b$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$b7652157-91a4-4584-925b-4ba0fbf4be4f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from the 1923 poem &ldquo;Black Finger&rdquo; by Angelina Weld Grimk&eacute;, a Black American writer. A cypress is a type of evergreen tree.</p>

<p style="padding-left:1em;">I have just seen a most beautiful thing,<br>Slim and still,<br>&ensp;Against a gold, gold sky,<br>&ensp;A straight black cypress,<br>Sensitive,<br>Exquisite,<br>A black finger<br>Pointing upwards.<br>Why, beautiful still finger, are you black?<br>And why are you pointing upwards?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ba40b8ab-740b-4359-8252-988146a38a2d","content":"<p>The speaker assesses a natural phenomenon, then questions the accuracy of her assessment.</p>"},{"id":"4e7f49b5-109e-4e10-97f0-774abcc0aef2","content":"<p>The speaker describes a distinctive sight in nature, then ponders what meaning to attribute to that sight.</p>"},{"id":"4a9c7205-7720-41fb-b081-6086d2061afb","content":"<p>The speaker presents an outdoor scene, then considers a human behavior occurring within that scene.</p>"},{"id":"2c8872fd-dc57-4ff2-8b3c-38834e575ea7","content":"<p>The speaker examines her surroundings, then speculates about their influence on her emotional state.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4e7f49b5-109e-4e10-97f0-774abcc0aef2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most accurately describes the overall structure of the text. First, the speaker describes observing a &ldquo;most beautiful&rdquo; sight: a tree (&ldquo;black cypress&rdquo;) standing out from the golden sky behind it, looking like a person&rsquo;s finger &ldquo;pointing upwards&rdquo; and appearing &ldquo;sensitive&rdquo; and &ldquo;exquisite.&rdquo; Then the speaker wonders about the image&rsquo;s meaning, asking why the finger is black and why it&rsquo;s pointing upward. Thus, the text moves from the speaker&rsquo;s description of a distinctive sight in nature to her pondering about what meaning to attribute to that sight. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the speaker assesses a natural sight&mdash;a &ldquo;black cypress&rdquo; tree standing &ldquo;against a gold, gold sky&rdquo; like a pointed finger&mdash;but doesn&rsquo;t question the accuracy of her own assessment. Although she wonders why the finger, which is really a tree, is black and why it&rsquo;s pointing, the speaker doesn&rsquo;t suggest that her belief that the tree resembles a finger is wrong. Choice C is incorrect. Although the speaker describes seeing a &ldquo;black cypress&rdquo; tree standing &ldquo;against a gold, gold sky&rdquo; like a pointed finger, she wonders about that natural image (asking why the finger, which is really a tree, is black and why it&rsquo;s pointing) and doesn&rsquo;t give any indication that any people are present in the scene. Choice D is incorrect. Although the speaker examines and wonders about one thing in her surroundings&mdash;a &ldquo;black cypress&rdquo; tree standing &ldquo;against a gold, gold sky&rdquo; like a pointed finger&mdash;she doesn&rsquo;t address her own emotional state or consider how it&rsquo;s affected by her surroundings. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-030-TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$8025312b-7c0f-4f97-9930-239c881a7f91$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"acb852e7","external_id":"5f5ee9b3-7025-41ae-ac00-71afc199772b","vaultid":"b7652157-91a4-4584-925b-4ba0fbf4be4f","uId":"393bfeee-c2e9-46ee-9345-cc936d64c420","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from the 1923 poem &ldquo;Black Finger&rdquo; by Angelina Weld Grimk&eacute;, a Black American writer. A cypress is a type of evergreen tree.</p>\n\n<p style=\"padding-left:1em;\">I have just seen a most beautiful thing,<br>Slim and still,<br>&ensp;Against a gold, gold sky,<br>&ensp;A straight black cypress,<br>Sensitive,<br>Exquisite,<br>A black finger<br>Pointing upwards.<br>Why, beautiful still finger, are you black?<br>And why are you pointing upwards?</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ba40b8ab-740b-4359-8252-988146a38a2d","content":"<p>The speaker assesses a natural phenomenon, then questions the accuracy of her assessment.</p>"},{"id":"4e7f49b5-109e-4e10-97f0-774abcc0aef2","content":"<p>The speaker describes a distinctive sight in nature, then ponders what meaning to attribute to that sight.</p>"},{"id":"4a9c7205-7720-41fb-b081-6086d2061afb","content":"<p>The speaker presents an outdoor scene, then considers a human behavior occurring within that scene.</p>"},{"id":"2c8872fd-dc57-4ff2-8b3c-38834e575ea7","content":"<p>The speaker examines her surroundings, then speculates about their influence on her emotional state.</p>"}],"keys":["4e7f49b5-109e-4e10-97f0-774abcc0aef2"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most accurately describes the overall structure of the text. First, the speaker describes observing a &ldquo;most beautiful&rdquo; sight: a tree (&ldquo;black cypress&rdquo;) standing out from the golden sky behind it, looking like a person&rsquo;s finger &ldquo;pointing upwards&rdquo; and appearing &ldquo;sensitive&rdquo; and &ldquo;exquisite.&rdquo; Then the speaker wonders about the image&rsquo;s meaning, asking why the finger is black and why it&rsquo;s pointing upward. Thus, the text moves from the speaker&rsquo;s description of a distinctive sight in nature to her pondering about what meaning to attribute to that sight. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the speaker assesses a natural sight&mdash;a &ldquo;black cypress&rdquo; tree standing &ldquo;against a gold, gold sky&rdquo; like a pointed finger&mdash;but doesn&rsquo;t question the accuracy of her own assessment. Although she wonders why the finger, which is really a tree, is black and why it&rsquo;s pointing, the speaker doesn&rsquo;t suggest that her belief that the tree resembles a finger is wrong. Choice C is incorrect. Although the speaker describes seeing a &ldquo;black cypress&rdquo; tree standing &ldquo;against a gold, gold sky&rdquo; like a pointed finger, she wonders about that natural image (asking why the finger, which is really a tree, is black and why it&rsquo;s pointing) and doesn&rsquo;t give any indication that any people are present in the scene. Choice D is incorrect. Although the speaker examines and wonders about one thing in her surroundings&mdash;a &ldquo;black cypress&rdquo; tree standing &ldquo;against a gold, gold sky&rdquo; like a pointed finger&mdash;she doesn&rsquo;t address her own emotional state or consider how it&rsquo;s affected by her surroundings. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-030-TSP","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"8025312b-7c0f-4f97-9930-239c881a7f91","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959319,"updateDate":1691007959319}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959319, 1691007959319),
    ($SATQ$ad4f7362$SATQ$, $SATQ$27085b71-998b-4e51-87b3-f4d637dd246c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from John Dryden&rsquo;s 1697 translation of Virgil&rsquo;s poem the <em>Aeneid</em>, written in the first century BCE. Queen Dido has just heard the Trojan hero Aeneas recount a sad tale.</p>
<blockquote class="dap_poemexcerpt">
<p>But anxious cares already seiz&rsquo;d the queen:</p>
<p>She fed within her veins a flame unseen;</p>
<p>The hero&rsquo;s valor, acts, and birth inspire</p>
<p>Her soul with love, and fan the secret fire.</p>
<p>His words, his looks, imprinted in her heart,</p>
<p>Improve the passion, and increase the smart.</p>
</blockquote>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"bbf37d93-f2ee-4b65-80fc-ea94327343ab","content":"<p>To indicate that Dido is hiding her skepticism of Aeneas&rsquo;s account</p>"},{"id":"d5689f5e-1ba8-4ad4-8b63-60d412d5813f","content":"<p>To emphasize that Dido has been deeply affected by Aeneas&rsquo;s story</p>"},{"id":"7829089b-6c20-4ef3-8047-f27d8bd72539","content":"<p>To imply that Dido engages both emotionally and intellectually with Aeneas</p>"},{"id":"3f72cbb2-0303-4338-93a7-5a1e781ba244","content":"<p>To suggest that Dido is worried that Aeneas might discover a secret she is keeping from him</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d5689f5e-1ba8-4ad4-8b63-60d412d5813f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most accurately describes the main purpose of the text, which is to foreground Queen Dido&rsquo;s strong emotional response to Aeneas&rsquo;s story. Throughout, the text emphasizes how deeply the queen is affected by both Aeneas&rsquo;s tale and persona. At the outset, the speaker explicitly states that "anxious cares...seiz&rsquo;d the queen" and then uses the metaphor of fire ("within her veins a flame unseen" and "secret fire") to evoke the warmth of Dido&rsquo;s feelings for Aeneas. In addition, the line "His words, his looks, imprinted in her heart" suggests the deep impression that Aeneas&rsquo;s story makes on Dido, eliciting passion for him ("improv[ing] the passion") and empathy for his suffering ("increas[ing] the smart").</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no indication in the text that Dido is skeptical of Aeneas&rsquo;s account, much less that she&rsquo;s trying to conceal that skepticism. On the contrary, the text shows her being moved by his words and developing feelings for him. Choice C is incorrect. While the text mentions that Dido is impressed by Aeneas&rsquo;s "valor, acts, and birth," which might suggest (but doesn&rsquo;t necessarily entail) intellectual engagement, the text doesn&rsquo;t represent Dido&rsquo;s engagement with Aeneas in a manner that suggests a balance between emotion and intellect. Rather, the text primarily emphasizes her emotional response&mdash;specifically her attraction to Aeneas and her emotional investment in his story, indicating that his "valor, acts, and birth inspire / Her soul with love, and fan the secret fire" and that his words and looks elicit passion and empathy. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Dido is worried about Aeneas discovering a secret she is concealing from him. Though the text begins by mentioning Dido&rsquo;s "anxious cares," this refers to her growing passion for Aeneas and pity for his suffering, not to worry about a secret she is concealing. The text&rsquo;s reference to a "flame unseen" and "secret fire" points to Dido&rsquo;s growing feelings for Aeneas that develop as he recounts his tale, not to a secret that existed before their encounter; moreover, the text provides no indication that Dido is worried Aeneas might discover these feelings.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ad4f7362","external_id":"27085b71-998b-4e51-87b3-f4d637dd246c","vaultid":null,"uId":"fa957156-8cc2-4f2e-9d24-170c33468451","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from John Dryden&rsquo;s 1697 translation of Virgil&rsquo;s poem the <em>Aeneid</em>, written in the first century BCE. Queen Dido has just heard the Trojan hero Aeneas recount a sad tale.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"dap_poemexcerpt\">\n<p>But anxious cares already seiz&rsquo;d the queen:</p>\n<p>She fed within her veins a flame unseen;</p>\n<p>The hero&rsquo;s valor, acts, and birth inspire</p>\n<p>Her soul with love, and fan the secret fire.</p>\n<p>His words, his looks, imprinted in her heart,</p>\n<p>Improve the passion, and increase the smart.</p>\n</blockquote>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"bbf37d93-f2ee-4b65-80fc-ea94327343ab","content":"<p>To indicate that Dido is hiding her skepticism of Aeneas&rsquo;s account</p>"},{"id":"d5689f5e-1ba8-4ad4-8b63-60d412d5813f","content":"<p>To emphasize that Dido has been deeply affected by Aeneas&rsquo;s story</p>"},{"id":"7829089b-6c20-4ef3-8047-f27d8bd72539","content":"<p>To imply that Dido engages both emotionally and intellectually with Aeneas</p>"},{"id":"3f72cbb2-0303-4338-93a7-5a1e781ba244","content":"<p>To suggest that Dido is worried that Aeneas might discover a secret she is keeping from him</p>"}],"keys":["d5689f5e-1ba8-4ad4-8b63-60d412d5813f"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most accurately describes the main purpose of the text, which is to foreground Queen Dido&rsquo;s strong emotional response to Aeneas&rsquo;s story. Throughout, the text emphasizes how deeply the queen is affected by both Aeneas&rsquo;s tale and persona. At the outset, the speaker explicitly states that \"anxious cares...seiz&rsquo;d the queen\" and then uses the metaphor of fire (\"within her veins a flame unseen\" and \"secret fire\") to evoke the warmth of Dido&rsquo;s feelings for Aeneas. In addition, the line \"His words, his looks, imprinted in her heart\" suggests the deep impression that Aeneas&rsquo;s story makes on Dido, eliciting passion for him (\"improv[ing] the passion\") and empathy for his suffering (\"increas[ing] the smart\").</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no indication in the text that Dido is skeptical of Aeneas&rsquo;s account, much less that she&rsquo;s trying to conceal that skepticism. On the contrary, the text shows her being moved by his words and developing feelings for him. Choice C is incorrect. While the text mentions that Dido is impressed by Aeneas&rsquo;s \"valor, acts, and birth,\" which might suggest (but doesn&rsquo;t necessarily entail) intellectual engagement, the text doesn&rsquo;t represent Dido&rsquo;s engagement with Aeneas in a manner that suggests a balance between emotion and intellect. Rather, the text primarily emphasizes her emotional response&mdash;specifically her attraction to Aeneas and her emotional investment in his story, indicating that his \"valor, acts, and birth inspire / Her soul with love, and fan the secret fire\" and that his words and looks elicit passion and empathy. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that Dido is worried about Aeneas discovering a secret she is concealing from him. Though the text begins by mentioning Dido&rsquo;s \"anxious cares,\" this refers to her growing passion for Aeneas and pity for his suffering, not to worry about a secret she is concealing. The text&rsquo;s reference to a \"flame unseen\" and \"secret fire\" points to Dido&rsquo;s growing feelings for Aeneas that develop as he recounts his tale, not to a secret that existed before their encounter; moreover, the text provides no indication that Dido is worried Aeneas might discover these feelings.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061176,"updateDate":1755117061176}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061176, 1755117061176),
    ($SATQ$adc8ea28$SATQ$, $SATQ$fe16e6f7-d37d-4568-9ff3-1c69bfc31d91$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The fossil remains of the individual known as Oase 1, discovered in Romania in 2002, can help paleoanthropologists not only <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> steps in the evolution of hominids but also illuminate the Pleistocene epoch generally, revealing important details about the time in which Oase 1 lived.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"51fff62a-d149-4aee-9dd3-d4ffc80aadfa","content":"<p>exploit</p>"},{"id":"c397fca2-5986-4e97-ba73-2f0ebe469dff","content":"<p>discern</p>"},{"id":"27545930-5010-4f42-b260-719fe80ef3f2","content":"<p>prioritize</p>"},{"id":"743b250b-b8a5-4c3c-a099-b9f5c6cf8096","content":"<p>yield</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c397fca2-5986-4e97-ba73-2f0ebe469dff"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the utility of the Oase 1 fossil to paleoanthropologists. As used in this context, "discern" means to detect or recognize something, especially something hidden or obscure. The text indicates that the Oase 1 fossil can help paleoanthropologists recognize patterns in the evolutionary process and shed light on ("illuminate") the period in which Oase 1 lived. Thus, the fossil will enable researchers to gain insights into, or discern, facts that are still not well understood.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because in this context, "exploit" would suggest that the paleoanthropologists are using "steps in the evolution of hominids," which does not make logical sense. Rather, the text is about how the Oase 1 fossil could help paleoanthropologists learn about hominid evolution and the Pleistocene epoch more generally. Choice C is incorrect because in this context, "prioritize" would suggest that either the paleoanthropologists are placing more importance on "steps in the evolution of hominids" than they are on something else not identified in the text or that they are placing these steps in some sort of order. Rather, the text is about how the Oase 1 fossil could help paleoanthropologists learn about hominid evolution and the Pleistocene epoch more generally. Choice D is incorrect because to say that paleoanthropologists could "yield" or generate "steps in the evolution of hominids" doesn&rsquo;t make sense. The researchers may develop new insights into those evolutionary steps, but they do not create those steps themselves. Rather, the context makes it clear that they are detecting or discovering patterns based on their study of the Oase 1 fossil.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"adc8ea28","external_id":"fe16e6f7-d37d-4568-9ff3-1c69bfc31d91","vaultid":null,"uId":"3adc2687-b720-4788-9353-d79d00d4684d","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The fossil remains of the individual known as Oase 1, discovered in Romania in 2002, can help paleoanthropologists not only <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> steps in the evolution of hominids but also illuminate the Pleistocene epoch generally, revealing important details about the time in which Oase 1 lived.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"51fff62a-d149-4aee-9dd3-d4ffc80aadfa","content":"<p>exploit</p>"},{"id":"c397fca2-5986-4e97-ba73-2f0ebe469dff","content":"<p>discern</p>"},{"id":"27545930-5010-4f42-b260-719fe80ef3f2","content":"<p>prioritize</p>"},{"id":"743b250b-b8a5-4c3c-a099-b9f5c6cf8096","content":"<p>yield</p>"}],"keys":["c397fca2-5986-4e97-ba73-2f0ebe469dff"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the utility of the Oase 1 fossil to paleoanthropologists. As used in this context, \"discern\" means to detect or recognize something, especially something hidden or obscure. The text indicates that the Oase 1 fossil can help paleoanthropologists recognize patterns in the evolutionary process and shed light on (\"illuminate\") the period in which Oase 1 lived. Thus, the fossil will enable researchers to gain insights into, or discern, facts that are still not well understood.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because in this context, \"exploit\" would suggest that the paleoanthropologists are using \"steps in the evolution of hominids,\" which does not make logical sense. Rather, the text is about how the Oase 1 fossil could help paleoanthropologists learn about hominid evolution and the Pleistocene epoch more generally. Choice C is incorrect because in this context, \"prioritize\" would suggest that either the paleoanthropologists are placing more importance on \"steps in the evolution of hominids\" than they are on something else not identified in the text or that they are placing these steps in some sort of order. Rather, the text is about how the Oase 1 fossil could help paleoanthropologists learn about hominid evolution and the Pleistocene epoch more generally. Choice D is incorrect because to say that paleoanthropologists could \"yield\" or generate \"steps in the evolution of hominids\" doesn&rsquo;t make sense. The researchers may develop new insights into those evolutionary steps, but they do not create those steps themselves. Rather, the context makes it clear that they are detecting or discovering patterns based on their study of the Oase 1 fossil.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061193,"updateDate":1755117061193}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061193, 1755117061193),
    ($SATQ$ae2b3112$SATQ$, $SATQ$eb9937bf-5401-4ef3-8267-1717cca62488$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$79cac8bd-2400-46f0-be62-e2e16f207bab$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>By combining Indigenous and classical music, Cree composer and cellist Cris Derksen creates works that reflect the diverse cultural landscape of Canada. For her album <em>Orchestral Powwow</em>, Derksen composed new songs in the style of traditional powwow music that were accompanied by classical arrangements played by an orchestra. But where an orchestra would normally follow the directions of a conductor, the musicians on <em>Orchestral Powwow</em> are led by the beat of a powwow drum.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a7a84a1b-5fb9-49eb-b5ca-ef9ab71dd46f","content":"<p>To examine how Derksen&rsquo;s musical compositions blend cultures</p>"},{"id":"74ceb2c2-7136-4bbe-9bc1-d1ee8b0edfcc","content":"<p>To argue that Derksen should be recognized for creating a new style of music</p>"},{"id":"6b0235ed-d824-4935-8254-517eab10c05b","content":"<p>To describe the difficulties Derksen encountered when producing her album</p>"},{"id":"7d06a8aa-8a88-4da7-bc43-3ae801241e32","content":"<p>To establish a contrast between Derksen&rsquo;s classical training and her Cree heritage&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a7a84a1b-5fb9-49eb-b5ca-ef9ab71dd46f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes the main purpose of the text, which is to discuss how Derksen&rsquo;s compositions incorporate elements from both Indigenous and classical music. After introducing Derksen, the text describes how the songs Derksen composed for her album <em>Orchestral Powwow</em> feature aspects of the two musical traditions. Specifically, the text notes that Derksen wrote songs in the style of traditional powwow music but accompanied them with classical arrangements played by an orchestra that followed the beat of a powwow drum rather than the directions of a conductor. In this way, Derksen&rsquo;s compositions blend different cultures. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because although the text suggests that Derksen&rsquo;s songs contain innovative elements since they blend styles from two different musical traditions, it doesn&rsquo;t discuss whether her compositions constitute a new style of music, let alone whether Derksen should be recognized for creating a new style of music.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t mention any difficulties Derksen encountered when producing her album. Rather, the text describes how the songs on the album exemplify how Derksen combines music from two different cultures.
&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because although the text mentions Derksen&rsquo;s Cree heritage and suggests that she relies on knowledge of both Indigenous and classical music when she composes her songs, it doesn&rsquo;t discuss her musical training. Additionally, the text is primarily focused on how Derksen combines different cultural traditions, not on contrasting Derksen&rsquo;s training with her heritage. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-012-TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$8f24d52e-9050-4df0-bf89-a7555cdd63e1$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ae2b3112","external_id":"eb9937bf-5401-4ef3-8267-1717cca62488","vaultid":"79cac8bd-2400-46f0-be62-e2e16f207bab","uId":"dfd0d4bc-5a39-4171-bf70-e1e20cdf53c7","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>By combining Indigenous and classical music, Cree composer and cellist Cris Derksen creates works that reflect the diverse cultural landscape of Canada. For her album <em>Orchestral Powwow</em>, Derksen composed new songs in the style of traditional powwow music that were accompanied by classical arrangements played by an orchestra. But where an orchestra would normally follow the directions of a conductor, the musicians on <em>Orchestral Powwow</em> are led by the beat of a powwow drum.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"a7a84a1b-5fb9-49eb-b5ca-ef9ab71dd46f","content":"<p>To examine how Derksen&rsquo;s musical compositions blend cultures</p>"},{"id":"74ceb2c2-7136-4bbe-9bc1-d1ee8b0edfcc","content":"<p>To argue that Derksen should be recognized for creating a new style of music</p>"},{"id":"6b0235ed-d824-4935-8254-517eab10c05b","content":"<p>To describe the difficulties Derksen encountered when producing her album</p>"},{"id":"7d06a8aa-8a88-4da7-bc43-3ae801241e32","content":"<p>To establish a contrast between Derksen&rsquo;s classical training and her Cree heritage&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["a7a84a1b-5fb9-49eb-b5ca-ef9ab71dd46f"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes the main purpose of the text, which is to discuss how Derksen&rsquo;s compositions incorporate elements from both Indigenous and classical music. After introducing Derksen, the text describes how the songs Derksen composed for her album <em>Orchestral Powwow</em> feature aspects of the two musical traditions. Specifically, the text notes that Derksen wrote songs in the style of traditional powwow music but accompanied them with classical arrangements played by an orchestra that followed the beat of a powwow drum rather than the directions of a conductor. In this way, Derksen&rsquo;s compositions blend different cultures. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect because although the text suggests that Derksen&rsquo;s songs contain innovative elements since they blend styles from two different musical traditions, it doesn&rsquo;t discuss whether her compositions constitute a new style of music, let alone whether Derksen should be recognized for creating a new style of music.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t mention any difficulties Derksen encountered when producing her album. Rather, the text describes how the songs on the album exemplify how Derksen combines music from two different cultures.\n&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because although the text mentions Derksen&rsquo;s Cree heritage and suggests that she relies on knowledge of both Indigenous and classical music when she composes her songs, it doesn&rsquo;t discuss her musical training. Additionally, the text is primarily focused on how Derksen combines different cultural traditions, not on contrasting Derksen&rsquo;s training with her heritage. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-012-TSP","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"8f24d52e-9050-4df0-bf89-a7555cdd63e1","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959314,"updateDate":1691007959314}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959314, 1691007959314),
    ($SATQ$af4300b0$SATQ$, $SATQ$d7668860-9878-4087-b476-e548f9b28d5f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The creation of Lotte Reiniger&rsquo;s 1926 animated film <em>The Adventures of Prince Achmed</em> was <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> process. Over the course of three years, Reiniger and her collaborators painstakingly made more than 250,000 individual images of hand-cut paper silhouettes and repeatedly had to invent entirely new methods and tools to create the special effects Reiniger envisioned.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"853aa74d-3938-4f39-859e-aa546835af0b","content":"<p>a haphazard</p>"},{"id":"3a6cc567-a316-48c4-be35-1359bf350c46","content":"<p>a contentious</p>"},{"id":"9172ede5-4a76-44ea-aee8-2fb25e1ff0ba","content":"<p>an ineffectual</p>"},{"id":"06cb84ce-e4ea-40b9-b05d-fab997afb3a0","content":"<p>an arduous</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["06cb84ce-e4ea-40b9-b05d-fab997afb3a0"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the creation of <em>The Adventures of Prince Achmed.</em> In this context, "arduous" means that the process is marked by great labor or effort. According to the text, the creation of the 1926 animated film <em>The Adventures of Prince Achmed</em> took three years and was a painstaking process. Since the process was so long and required great efforts by Lotte Reiniger and her team, the creation of the film was therefore an arduous process.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate that the creation of Reiniger&rsquo;s film was "a haphazard," or disorganized, process. In fact, the text suggests that the creation process was quite meticulous and the team worked hard together to produce the envisioned effects. Choice B is incorrect. While the text does suggest that the creation of Reiniger&rsquo;s film was a long and difficult process, it doesn&rsquo;t suggest that the process was "a contentious" one, or one causing controversy or argument. The text suggests that the team worked together to produce the envisioned effects. Choice C is incorrect because rather than describing the process of creating the film as "ineffectual," or not having the effect it was intended to have, the text describes the process as ultimately successful despite the difficulty it involved.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"af4300b0","external_id":"d7668860-9878-4087-b476-e548f9b28d5f","vaultid":null,"uId":"276c3108-717a-46fc-86eb-a6953b69fdb0","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The creation of Lotte Reiniger&rsquo;s 1926 animated film <em>The Adventures of Prince Achmed</em> was <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> process. Over the course of three years, Reiniger and her collaborators painstakingly made more than 250,000 individual images of hand-cut paper silhouettes and repeatedly had to invent entirely new methods and tools to create the special effects Reiniger envisioned.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"853aa74d-3938-4f39-859e-aa546835af0b","content":"<p>a haphazard</p>"},{"id":"3a6cc567-a316-48c4-be35-1359bf350c46","content":"<p>a contentious</p>"},{"id":"9172ede5-4a76-44ea-aee8-2fb25e1ff0ba","content":"<p>an ineffectual</p>"},{"id":"06cb84ce-e4ea-40b9-b05d-fab997afb3a0","content":"<p>an arduous</p>"}],"keys":["06cb84ce-e4ea-40b9-b05d-fab997afb3a0"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the creation of <em>The Adventures of Prince Achmed.</em> In this context, \"arduous\" means that the process is marked by great labor or effort. According to the text, the creation of the 1926 animated film <em>The Adventures of Prince Achmed</em> took three years and was a painstaking process. Since the process was so long and required great efforts by Lotte Reiniger and her team, the creation of the film was therefore an arduous process.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate that the creation of Reiniger&rsquo;s film was \"a haphazard,\" or disorganized, process. In fact, the text suggests that the creation process was quite meticulous and the team worked hard together to produce the envisioned effects. Choice B is incorrect. While the text does suggest that the creation of Reiniger&rsquo;s film was a long and difficult process, it doesn&rsquo;t suggest that the process was \"a contentious\" one, or one causing controversy or argument. The text suggests that the team worked together to produce the envisioned effects. Choice C is incorrect because rather than describing the process of creating the film as \"ineffectual,\" or not having the effect it was intended to have, the text describes the process as ultimately successful despite the difficulty it involved.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669213,"updateDate":1743430669213}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669213, 1743430669213),
    ($SATQ$af43b0bd$SATQ$, $SATQ$1ac31154-0bb8-4bee-bd86-75ce7ce0ba63$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Researchers have long hypothesized that woolly mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with grooved tips known as Clovis points. One anthropologist set out to test this hypothesis. Using a mechanical spear-thrower, he launched spears with Clovis points into mounds of clay&mdash;substitutes for the animals&rsquo; large bodies. The projectiles generally penetrated only a few inches into the clay, an amount insufficient to have harmed most woolly mammoths. This led the anthropologist to conclude that hunters using spears with Clovis points likely weren&rsquo;t the principal drivers of the extinction.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"31a0c468-dcee-41f6-b54d-f1ba717cc72b","content":"<p>To argue for the significance of new findings amid an ongoing debate among researchers</p>"},{"id":"9e75e012-c210-452b-942a-4559b08e15f2","content":"<p>To discuss the advantages and disadvantages of the method used in an experiment</p>"},{"id":"f0263b11-565d-4ac4-b847-54b468170fe1","content":"<p>To summarize two competing hypotheses and a major finding associated with each one</p>"},{"id":"06585c1a-060c-4f67-96e6-14c06baf3859","content":"<p>To describe an experiment whose results cast doubt on an established hypothesis</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["06585c1a-060c-4f67-96e6-14c06baf3859"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most accurately states the main purpose of the text, which is to describe an experiment whose results cast doubt on an established hypothesis. The text begins by noting that researchers have long believed that woolly mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with Clovis points. The text then describes an experiment conducted by an anthropologist to test this hypothesis. According to the text, the results of the experiment led the anthropologist to conclude that hunters using spears with Clovis points likely weren&rsquo;t the primary cause of the extinction. The anthropologist&rsquo;s results cast doubt on the long-held hypothesis presented at the beginning of the text and suggest that woolly mammoths may have become extinct in North America due to some other cause.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that researchers have been involved in an ongoing debate. On the contrary, the text suggests that most researchers agree on the cause of the woolly mammoth&rsquo;s extinction in North America. Choice B is incorrect because the text never mentions any advantages or disadvantages of the method used in the experiment, focusing instead on the results achieved using that method. Choice C is incorrect because the text addresses only one hypothesis, that mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with Clovis points. Rather than present a competing hypothesis, the text explains how one anthropologist designed an experiment to test this long-held hypothesis.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"af43b0bd","external_id":"1ac31154-0bb8-4bee-bd86-75ce7ce0ba63","vaultid":null,"uId":"a60a2428-46a8-48e8-a14d-997cb9b1d0c8","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Researchers have long hypothesized that woolly mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with grooved tips known as Clovis points. One anthropologist set out to test this hypothesis. Using a mechanical spear-thrower, he launched spears with Clovis points into mounds of clay&mdash;substitutes for the animals&rsquo; large bodies. The projectiles generally penetrated only a few inches into the clay, an amount insufficient to have harmed most woolly mammoths. This led the anthropologist to conclude that hunters using spears with Clovis points likely weren&rsquo;t the principal drivers of the extinction.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"31a0c468-dcee-41f6-b54d-f1ba717cc72b","content":"<p>To argue for the significance of new findings amid an ongoing debate among researchers</p>"},{"id":"9e75e012-c210-452b-942a-4559b08e15f2","content":"<p>To discuss the advantages and disadvantages of the method used in an experiment</p>"},{"id":"f0263b11-565d-4ac4-b847-54b468170fe1","content":"<p>To summarize two competing hypotheses and a major finding associated with each one</p>"},{"id":"06585c1a-060c-4f67-96e6-14c06baf3859","content":"<p>To describe an experiment whose results cast doubt on an established hypothesis</p>"}],"keys":["06585c1a-060c-4f67-96e6-14c06baf3859"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most accurately states the main purpose of the text, which is to describe an experiment whose results cast doubt on an established hypothesis. The text begins by noting that researchers have long believed that woolly mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with Clovis points. The text then describes an experiment conducted by an anthropologist to test this hypothesis. According to the text, the results of the experiment led the anthropologist to conclude that hunters using spears with Clovis points likely weren&rsquo;t the primary cause of the extinction. The anthropologist&rsquo;s results cast doubt on the long-held hypothesis presented at the beginning of the text and suggest that woolly mammoths may have become extinct in North America due to some other cause.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that researchers have been involved in an ongoing debate. On the contrary, the text suggests that most researchers agree on the cause of the woolly mammoth&rsquo;s extinction in North America. Choice B is incorrect because the text never mentions any advantages or disadvantages of the method used in the experiment, focusing instead on the results achieved using that method. Choice C is incorrect because the text addresses only one hypothesis, that mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with Clovis points. Rather than present a competing hypothesis, the text explains how one anthropologist designed an experiment to test this long-held hypothesis.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323032,"updateDate":1730147323032}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323032, 1730147323032),
    ($SATQ$afd2a9eb$SATQ$, $SATQ$11826936-eafe-4e3e-bffc-413f20fc3a51$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Manul cats are small, shy felines. They live mostly alone in out-of-the-way parts of Asia, such as on Mount Everest. These cats have been difficult to research because their habitats are so <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> large populations of humans.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c8027248-b76b-4098-981c-feb4d4bef769","content":"<p>full of</p>"},{"id":"5598e170-3903-486d-baef-088d58e28d6b","content":"<p>drawn to</p>"},{"id":"20cd04eb-de1b-41eb-a909-58193d33b052","content":"<p>responsible for</p>"},{"id":"aceaadb2-2878-49a6-befd-dc4444b2845d","content":"<p>distant from</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["aceaadb2-2878-49a6-befd-dc4444b2845d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of manul cats. The text states that manul cats live in "out-of-the-way parts of Asia" (citing the famously remote Mount Everest as an example) and indicates that it is difficult to research the cats because of the location of their habitats. By emphasizing that the habitats are remote in relation to humans, the text conveys that being "distant from," or far from, large groups of humans makes manul cats challenging to study.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because saying that the habitats of manul cats are "full of large populations of humans" would indicate that the cats cohabitate with many humans, which would directly contradict the text&rsquo;s claim that the cats live in "out-of-the-way" areas. Choice B is incorrect because the missing words describe an aspect of manul cats&rsquo; habitats, or the areas where they live, and it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that areas could be "drawn to," or attracted by, large groups of humans. Choice C is incorrect. In this context, "responsible for" would mean either having an obligation to care for something or being the cause of something, and it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that the habitats of manul cats (the areas where the cats live) would need to care for humans or that the habitats somehow created large human populations.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"afd2a9eb","external_id":"11826936-eafe-4e3e-bffc-413f20fc3a51","vaultid":null,"uId":"686b6d63-c215-44bb-86ae-bf7e378ff8df","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Manul cats are small, shy felines. They live mostly alone in out-of-the-way parts of Asia, such as on Mount Everest. These cats have been difficult to research because their habitats are so <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> large populations of humans.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c8027248-b76b-4098-981c-feb4d4bef769","content":"<p>full of</p>"},{"id":"5598e170-3903-486d-baef-088d58e28d6b","content":"<p>drawn to</p>"},{"id":"20cd04eb-de1b-41eb-a909-58193d33b052","content":"<p>responsible for</p>"},{"id":"aceaadb2-2878-49a6-befd-dc4444b2845d","content":"<p>distant from</p>"}],"keys":["aceaadb2-2878-49a6-befd-dc4444b2845d"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of manul cats. The text states that manul cats live in \"out-of-the-way parts of Asia\" (citing the famously remote Mount Everest as an example) and indicates that it is difficult to research the cats because of the location of their habitats. By emphasizing that the habitats are remote in relation to humans, the text conveys that being \"distant from,\" or far from, large groups of humans makes manul cats challenging to study.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because saying that the habitats of manul cats are \"full of large populations of humans\" would indicate that the cats cohabitate with many humans, which would directly contradict the text&rsquo;s claim that the cats live in \"out-of-the-way\" areas. Choice B is incorrect because the missing words describe an aspect of manul cats&rsquo; habitats, or the areas where they live, and it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that areas could be \"drawn to,\" or attracted by, large groups of humans. Choice C is incorrect. In this context, \"responsible for\" would mean either having an obligation to care for something or being the cause of something, and it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that the habitats of manul cats (the areas where the cats live) would need to care for humans or that the habitats somehow created large human populations.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323040,"updateDate":1730147323040}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323040, 1730147323040),
    ($SATQ$afd48140$SATQ$, $SATQ$0524fed6-0b7e-4b79-ab77-46395a4aba62$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$45534c9a-97d4-46bc-8f54-8bee378e131d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In 1877, 85% of California&rsquo;s railways were already controlled by the Southern Pacific Railroad. The company further solidified its <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> in rail access to the state&rsquo;s Pacific coast when it completed the Sunset Route in 1883: running from Louisiana to Southern California, the route established the first transcontinental rail line across the southern United States.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2c306945-bfbb-4569-82ff-5bd592b03599","content":"<p>dominance</p>"},{"id":"cd568a3d-9122-45ba-b15e-9761f9ea4f27","content":"<p>creativity</p>"},{"id":"3b8f4ae1-47ba-4c5b-831b-a6502c75260f","content":"<p>insignificance</p>"},{"id":"2286284d-e5c1-4014-bd13-49f9582d613c","content":"<p>neutrality</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2c306945-bfbb-4569-82ff-5bd592b03599"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most logically and precisely completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the Southern Pacific Railroad. As used in this context, "dominance" means the state of being more successful than others. The text states that the Southern Pacific Railroad already controlled 85% of California&rsquo;s railways in 1877, and that the Sunset Route it constructed in 1883 was the first transcontinental rail line across the southern United States. Therefore, the Southern Pacific Railroad would be more successful than other railroads in the area, and the construction of the Sunset Route would further solidify its dominance in rail access to California&rsquo;s coast.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although the construction of the Sunset Route must have required some creativity, or use of imagination, the word "creativity" would not also encompass the fact that the Southern Pacific Railroad already controlled 85% of California&rsquo;s railways. The text is more focused on the railroad&rsquo;s control of the field and overall success rather than its imaginative thought processes. Choice C is incorrect because if the Southern Pacific Railroad controlled the majority of California&rsquo;s railways, it would not make sense to refer to its "insignificance," or the state of being unimportant. Rather, the opposite would be true. Choice D is incorrect because in context it would not make sense to refer to the Southern Pacific Railroad&rsquo;s "neutrality," or absence of strong opinion on a matter, since no opinions are mentioned. Nor would "neutrality" in the sense of impartiality in a conflict be a logical or precise choice since no conflict is explicitly described. There might be an implied conflict between the Southern Pacific Railroad and other railroads doing business in California, but that is not a conflict in which the Southern Pacific Railroad would take an impartial position.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-050-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$61cbbb67-f6b2-48d2-9553-e56d31c51a23$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"afd48140","external_id":"0524fed6-0b7e-4b79-ab77-46395a4aba62","vaultid":"45534c9a-97d4-46bc-8f54-8bee378e131d","uId":"555204f7-b2e5-4207-b94b-31709c8486c8","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In 1877, 85% of California&rsquo;s railways were already controlled by the Southern Pacific Railroad. The company further solidified its <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> in rail access to the state&rsquo;s Pacific coast when it completed the Sunset Route in 1883: running from Louisiana to Southern California, the route established the first transcontinental rail line across the southern United States.&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2c306945-bfbb-4569-82ff-5bd592b03599","content":"<p>dominance</p>"},{"id":"cd568a3d-9122-45ba-b15e-9761f9ea4f27","content":"<p>creativity</p>"},{"id":"3b8f4ae1-47ba-4c5b-831b-a6502c75260f","content":"<p>insignificance</p>"},{"id":"2286284d-e5c1-4014-bd13-49f9582d613c","content":"<p>neutrality</p>"}],"keys":["2c306945-bfbb-4569-82ff-5bd592b03599"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most logically and precisely completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the Southern Pacific Railroad. As used in this context, \"dominance\" means the state of being more successful than others. The text states that the Southern Pacific Railroad already controlled 85% of California&rsquo;s railways in 1877, and that the Sunset Route it constructed in 1883 was the first transcontinental rail line across the southern United States. Therefore, the Southern Pacific Railroad would be more successful than other railroads in the area, and the construction of the Sunset Route would further solidify its dominance in rail access to California&rsquo;s coast.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although the construction of the Sunset Route must have required some creativity, or use of imagination, the word \"creativity\" would not also encompass the fact that the Southern Pacific Railroad already controlled 85% of California&rsquo;s railways. The text is more focused on the railroad&rsquo;s control of the field and overall success rather than its imaginative thought processes. Choice C is incorrect because if the Southern Pacific Railroad controlled the majority of California&rsquo;s railways, it would not make sense to refer to its \"insignificance,\" or the state of being unimportant. Rather, the opposite would be true. Choice D is incorrect because in context it would not make sense to refer to the Southern Pacific Railroad&rsquo;s \"neutrality,\" or absence of strong opinion on a matter, since no opinions are mentioned. Nor would \"neutrality\" in the sense of impartiality in a conflict be a logical or precise choice since no conflict is explicitly described. There might be an implied conflict between the Southern Pacific Railroad and other railroads doing business in California, but that is not a conflict in which the Southern Pacific Railroad would take an impartial position.</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-050-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"61cbbb67-f6b2-48d2-9553-e56d31c51a23","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959324,"updateDate":1691007959324}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959324, 1691007959324),
    ($SATQ$b0ea8c28$SATQ$, $SATQ$7c826b0e-e21f-4bac-b7fe-047b231f7ca1$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ea030d78-8e1b-4d61-ad0a-5211cdb9e5e8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><em>Sue&ntilde;o de Familia</em> is an exhibition of drawings, paintings, and ceramics that explores the artistic heritage of US-based artist Yolanda Gonz&aacute;lez. The exhibition <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> five generations, featuring works by Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s great-grandfather, grandmother, mother, and niece as well as Gonz&aacute;lez herself.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"fe4abdcc-4f7b-4eda-bebd-185a197f3d80","content":"<p>borrows</p>"},{"id":"63d7144f-a067-413e-9442-5718b8c2a9fc","content":"<p>spans</p>"},{"id":"fa62374b-7f67-4c7d-93fa-beed4cb62cbd","content":"<p>judges</p>"},{"id":"af88f7bf-6343-4bcf-b846-0087fc8a5072","content":"<p>neglects</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["63d7144f-a067-413e-9442-5718b8c2a9fc"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the <em>Sue&ntilde;o de Familia</em> art exhibition. In this context, &ldquo;spans&rdquo; means extends across or covers. The text states that the exhibition explores Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s artistic heritage and features artwork by her great-grandfather, grandmother, mother, and niece. This context conveys the idea that the exhibition spans, or extends across, five generations of Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s family. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that the exhibition &ldquo;borrows,&rdquo; or acquires, five generations of Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s family. The text indicates that the exhibition features artwork by family members from five generations, not that the five generations themselves have been acquired for inclusion in the exhibition. Choice C is incorrect because the text indicates that the purpose of the exhibition is to highlight artwork, not to &ldquo;judge,&rdquo; or give an opinion on, five generations of the artist&rsquo;s family. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that the exhibition &ldquo;neglects,&rdquo; or gives little attention to, five generations of Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s family. On the contrary, the text indicates that the exhibition is dedicated to exploring Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s artistic heritage and therefore designed to bring attention to her family members and their artwork. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-042-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$5250bba8-f594-4b8a-b9a9-915767021517$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b0ea8c28","external_id":"7c826b0e-e21f-4bac-b7fe-047b231f7ca1","vaultid":"ea030d78-8e1b-4d61-ad0a-5211cdb9e5e8","uId":"9c0645e8-a87b-4844-b5f4-4550adec1f4a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p><em>Sue&ntilde;o de Familia</em> is an exhibition of drawings, paintings, and ceramics that explores the artistic heritage of US-based artist Yolanda Gonz&aacute;lez. The exhibition <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> five generations, featuring works by Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s great-grandfather, grandmother, mother, and niece as well as Gonz&aacute;lez herself.&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"fe4abdcc-4f7b-4eda-bebd-185a197f3d80","content":"<p>borrows</p>"},{"id":"63d7144f-a067-413e-9442-5718b8c2a9fc","content":"<p>spans</p>"},{"id":"fa62374b-7f67-4c7d-93fa-beed4cb62cbd","content":"<p>judges</p>"},{"id":"af88f7bf-6343-4bcf-b846-0087fc8a5072","content":"<p>neglects</p>"}],"keys":["63d7144f-a067-413e-9442-5718b8c2a9fc"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the <em>Sue&ntilde;o de Familia</em> art exhibition. In this context, &ldquo;spans&rdquo; means extends across or covers. The text states that the exhibition explores Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s artistic heritage and features artwork by her great-grandfather, grandmother, mother, and niece. This context conveys the idea that the exhibition spans, or extends across, five generations of Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s family. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that the exhibition &ldquo;borrows,&rdquo; or acquires, five generations of Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s family. The text indicates that the exhibition features artwork by family members from five generations, not that the five generations themselves have been acquired for inclusion in the exhibition. Choice C is incorrect because the text indicates that the purpose of the exhibition is to highlight artwork, not to &ldquo;judge,&rdquo; or give an opinion on, five generations of the artist&rsquo;s family. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that the exhibition &ldquo;neglects,&rdquo; or gives little attention to, five generations of Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s family. On the contrary, the text indicates that the exhibition is dedicated to exploring Gonz&aacute;lez&rsquo;s artistic heritage and therefore designed to bring attention to her family members and their artwork. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-042-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"5250bba8-f594-4b8a-b9a9-915767021517","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959322,"updateDate":1691007959322}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959322, 1691007959322),
    ($SATQ$b0f7541b$SATQ$, $SATQ$88b3e233-c118-413a-b65c-fc38699130a8$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$9687ede1-6f38-4118-b9bb-0bf37c0bb19d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is adapted from Herman Melville&rsquo;s 1857 novel <em>The Confidence-Man</em>. Humphry Davy was a prominent British chemist and inventor.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Years ago, a grave American savant, being in London, observed at an evening party there, a certain coxcombical fellow, as he thought, an absurd ribbon in his lapel, and full of smart [banter], whisking about to the admiration of as many as were disposed to admire. Great was the savant&rsquo;s disdain; but, chancing ere long to find himself in a corner with the jackanapes, got into conversation with him, when he was somewhat ill-prepared for the good sense of the jackanapes, but was altogether thrown aback, upon subsequently being [informed that he was] no less a personage than Sir Humphry Davy.</p>
</blockquote>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"62e3fdf1-394c-4105-adcc-d75360232ade","content":"<p>It portrays the thoughts of a character who is embarrassed about his own behavior.</p>"},{"id":"e7ec5f99-9ac5-4032-b647-608c053b5934","content":"<p>It presents an account of a misunderstanding.</p>"},{"id":"14553fec-9924-4399-b929-33517f1cb915","content":"<p>It offers a short history of how a person came to be famous.</p>"},{"id":"bfd93afc-9b5d-4094-bf54-2e46d09d145c","content":"<p>It explains why one character dislikes another.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e7ec5f99-9ac5-4032-b647-608c053b5934"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text tells a story of a first impression that turned out to be wrong: a serious American savant was dismissive of a goofy-looking, wisecracking guest at a British party, and then was shocked to learn that the guest was actually a prominent British chemist and inventor.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This is too strong and too narrow. Only at the very end is the savant "thrown aback" by the fact that the man was Sir Humphry Davy&mdash;he&rsquo;s not "embarrassed about his own behavior." Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the main purpose. The text never provides the history of how Sir Humphry Davy came to be famous. Nor does it provide any history for the American savant. Choice D is incorrect. This is too narrow. It doesn&rsquo;t include the second half of the text, where the savant gets into a conversation with the man and then finds out that the man is Sir Humphry Davy.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TSP-H001$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$9b7f38cc-ce34-4bd0-801b-d2bb23b5a50d$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b0f7541b","external_id":"88b3e233-c118-413a-b65c-fc38699130a8","vaultid":"9687ede1-6f38-4118-b9bb-0bf37c0bb19d","uId":"2524d8f3-37eb-4f4b-8aff-8fc1f38cc2e1","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is adapted from Herman Melville&rsquo;s 1857 novel <em>The Confidence-Man</em>. Humphry Davy was a prominent British chemist and inventor.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Years ago, a grave American savant, being in London, observed at an evening party there, a certain coxcombical fellow, as he thought, an absurd ribbon in his lapel, and full of smart [banter], whisking about to the admiration of as many as were disposed to admire. Great was the savant&rsquo;s disdain; but, chancing ere long to find himself in a corner with the jackanapes, got into conversation with him, when he was somewhat ill-prepared for the good sense of the jackanapes, but was altogether thrown aback, upon subsequently being [informed that he was] no less a personage than Sir Humphry Davy.</p>\n</blockquote>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"62e3fdf1-394c-4105-adcc-d75360232ade","content":"<p>It portrays the thoughts of a character who is embarrassed about his own behavior.</p>"},{"id":"e7ec5f99-9ac5-4032-b647-608c053b5934","content":"<p>It presents an account of a misunderstanding.</p>"},{"id":"14553fec-9924-4399-b929-33517f1cb915","content":"<p>It offers a short history of how a person came to be famous.</p>"},{"id":"bfd93afc-9b5d-4094-bf54-2e46d09d145c","content":"<p>It explains why one character dislikes another.</p>"}],"keys":["e7ec5f99-9ac5-4032-b647-608c053b5934"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text tells a story of a first impression that turned out to be wrong: a serious American savant was dismissive of a goofy-looking, wisecracking guest at a British party, and then was shocked to learn that the guest was actually a prominent British chemist and inventor.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This is too strong and too narrow. Only at the very end is the savant \"thrown aback\" by the fact that the man was Sir Humphry Davy&mdash;he&rsquo;s not \"embarrassed about his own behavior.\" Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the main purpose. The text never provides the history of how Sir Humphry Davy came to be famous. Nor does it provide any history for the American savant. Choice D is incorrect. This is too narrow. It doesn&rsquo;t include the second half of the text, where the savant gets into a conversation with the man and then finds out that the man is Sir Humphry Davy.</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TSP-H001","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"9b7f38cc-ce34-4bd0-801b-d2bb23b5a50d","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959375,"updateDate":1691007959375}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959375, 1691007959375),
    ($SATQ$b11bb2a3$SATQ$, $SATQ$07b3f7e5-e57c-4a76-be24-674638b5d65c$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$1b452255-da0d-4e92-9c7a-30394b79b3c6$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is adapted from Amy Lowell&rsquo;s 1912 poem &ldquo;Summer.&rdquo;</p>
<blockquote class="dap_poemexcerpt">
<p>It is summer, glorious, deep-toned summer,</p>
<p>The very crown of nature&rsquo;s changing year</p>
<p>When all her surging life is at its full.</p>
<p>To me alone it is a time of pause,</p>
<p><span role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content"><u>A void</u></span> and silent space between two worlds,</p>
<p>When inspiration lags, and feeling sleeps,</p>
<p>Gathering strength for efforts yet to come.</p>
</blockquote>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As used in the text, what does the phrase &ldquo;a void&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c9f8d142-5604-45bf-9c1b-5823de80d17c","content":"<p>A useless</p>"},{"id":"4a06ecbb-3065-485a-a9b9-1524ceda8b6a","content":"<p>An empty</p>"},{"id":"280f7da7-b8a6-40ba-8daa-f20e9c8428a8","content":"<p>A forgotten</p>"},{"id":"70651206-84cc-4827-b5c4-178c6ec44506","content":"<p>An incomplete</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4a06ecbb-3065-485a-a9b9-1524ceda8b6a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because as used in the text, a span of time is described as "a void" space, which most nearly means an empty or vacant one. In the text, the speaker describes summertime in counterintuitive terms: although nature&rsquo;s "surging life is at its full" during the season, the speaker feels summer to be "a time of pause, / A void and silent space between two worlds." The speaker says further that during summer, "feeling sleeps / Gathering strength" for future efforts. Thus, the speaker regards summer as an empty stretch of time, to be followed by a period of greater activity.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although the text does present summer as a time of inactivity, it doesn&rsquo;t characterize that inactivity as useless, or as having no purpose; in fact, the speaker regards summer as a time when "feeling" gathers "strength for efforts yet to come." Choice C is incorrect. Although the text characterizes summer as a time "when inspiration lags, and feeling sleeps," it doesn&rsquo;t discuss the season&rsquo;s relationship to the speaker&rsquo;s memory or suggest that summer can easily be forgotten. Choice D is incorrect. In some contexts, "void" can mean devoid of, or lacking, a particular element, and such a lack could be conceived of as incompleteness. However, the text doesn&rsquo;t portray summer as not being complete or whole; instead, it characterizes vacancy or inactivity as being an essential quality of the season, as experienced by the speaker.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-038-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$bada61b3-1925-40df-ba41-9f67e9bc97d6$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b11bb2a3","external_id":"07b3f7e5-e57c-4a76-be24-674638b5d65c","vaultid":"1b452255-da0d-4e92-9c7a-30394b79b3c6","uId":"d57f3db2-3616-4aa8-8daf-b6e75ec8dd1f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is adapted from Amy Lowell&rsquo;s 1912 poem &ldquo;Summer.&rdquo;</p>\n<blockquote class=\"dap_poemexcerpt\">\n<p>It is summer, glorious, deep-toned summer,</p>\n<p>The very crown of nature&rsquo;s changing year</p>\n<p>When all her surging life is at its full.</p>\n<p>To me alone it is a time of pause,</p>\n<p><span role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\"><u>A void</u></span> and silent space between two worlds,</p>\n<p>When inspiration lags, and feeling sleeps,</p>\n<p>Gathering strength for efforts yet to come.</p>\n</blockquote>","stem":"<p>As used in the text, what does the phrase &ldquo;a void&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c9f8d142-5604-45bf-9c1b-5823de80d17c","content":"<p>A useless</p>"},{"id":"4a06ecbb-3065-485a-a9b9-1524ceda8b6a","content":"<p>An empty</p>"},{"id":"280f7da7-b8a6-40ba-8daa-f20e9c8428a8","content":"<p>A forgotten</p>"},{"id":"70651206-84cc-4827-b5c4-178c6ec44506","content":"<p>An incomplete</p>"}],"keys":["4a06ecbb-3065-485a-a9b9-1524ceda8b6a"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because as used in the text, a span of time is described as \"a void\" space, which most nearly means an empty or vacant one. In the text, the speaker describes summertime in counterintuitive terms: although nature&rsquo;s \"surging life is at its full\" during the season, the speaker feels summer to be \"a time of pause, / A void and silent space between two worlds.\" The speaker says further that during summer, \"feeling sleeps / Gathering strength\" for future efforts. Thus, the speaker regards summer as an empty stretch of time, to be followed by a period of greater activity.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although the text does present summer as a time of inactivity, it doesn&rsquo;t characterize that inactivity as useless, or as having no purpose; in fact, the speaker regards summer as a time when \"feeling\" gathers \"strength for efforts yet to come.\" Choice C is incorrect. Although the text characterizes summer as a time \"when inspiration lags, and feeling sleeps,\" it doesn&rsquo;t discuss the season&rsquo;s relationship to the speaker&rsquo;s memory or suggest that summer can easily be forgotten. Choice D is incorrect. In some contexts, \"void\" can mean devoid of, or lacking, a particular element, and such a lack could be conceived of as incompleteness. However, the text doesn&rsquo;t portray summer as not being complete or whole; instead, it characterizes vacancy or inactivity as being an essential quality of the season, as experienced by the speaker.</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-038-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"bada61b3-1925-40df-ba41-9f67e9bc97d6","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959321,"updateDate":1691007959321}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959321, 1691007959321),
    ($SATQ$b13378c8$SATQ$, $SATQ$19d37226-360f-4850-89ea-9e75cd0875fb$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$e40c7b81-fba3-481e-aa00-9293b60ba388$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Early in the Great Migration of 1910&ndash;1970, which involved the mass migration of Black people from the southern to the northern United States, political activist and <em>Chicago Defender</em> writer Fannie Barrier Williams was instrumental in helping other Black women establish themselves in the North. Many women hoped for better employment opportunities in the North because, in the South, they faced much competition for domestic employment and men tended to get agricultural work. To aid with this transition, Barrier Williams helped secure job placement in the North for many women before they even began their journey.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9a1231f9-ecfe-45cd-958a-fb4eeba317b6","content":"<p>To introduce and illustrate Barrier Williams&rsquo;s integral role in supporting other Black women as their circumstances changed during part of the Great Migration</p>"},{"id":"8b7fde5f-9fb7-4836-9d75-40f313745d33","content":"<p>To establish that Barrier Williams used her professional connections to arrange employment for other Black women, including jobs with the <em>Chicago Defender</em></p>"},{"id":"e936678b-f1e7-4838-aa45-654285051630","content":"<p>To demonstrate that the factors that motivated the start of the Great Migration were different for Black women than they were for Black men</p>"},{"id":"e2dc5020-ed02-4195-afc9-9aae00c4d661","content":"<p>To provide an overview of the employment challenges faced by Black women in the agricultural and domestic spheres in the southern United States</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9a1231f9-ecfe-45cd-958a-fb4eeba317b6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes the text&rsquo;s purpose, which is to discuss the important role Barrier Williams played in supporting many other Black women as they relocated to the northern United States during the early years of the Great Migration. After introducing Barrier Williams, the text describes how she helped find jobs for other Black women, who in many cases relocated in search of better employment prospects than the South could offer at the time. The text indicates that by doing so, she eased these women&rsquo;s transition as their circumstances changed. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although the text mentions Barrier Williams&rsquo;s work as a political activist and writer for the <em>Chicago Defender</em>, it doesn&rsquo;t discuss any professional connections she made in these roles or indicate that she used any such connections in her work to secure employment for other Black women. Choice C is incorrect. Although the text discusses a factor that caused many women to relocate during the Great Migration, their difficulty finding employment in the South, the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate that this factor motivated the start of the Great Migration. Moreover, the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss the factors that motivated Black men to migrate. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text mentions the difficult employment prospects for Black women in the domestic and agricultural sectors in the South during the Great Migration, the text&rsquo;s main purpose isn&rsquo;t to provide an overview of the employment challenges Black women faced in these sectors. Rather, it provides this information to show that Barrier Williams played a crucial role in supporting many Black women who relocated to the North by helping them achieve one of their main goals, securing a job. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-051-TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$a5ab3a5a-be7a-4eb1-a287-41cdefdcc610$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b13378c8","external_id":"19d37226-360f-4850-89ea-9e75cd0875fb","vaultid":"e40c7b81-fba3-481e-aa00-9293b60ba388","uId":"09c41447-e1f1-4921-a393-2e9aa2a61bc1","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Early in the Great Migration of 1910&ndash;1970, which involved the mass migration of Black people from the southern to the northern United States, political activist and <em>Chicago Defender</em> writer Fannie Barrier Williams was instrumental in helping other Black women establish themselves in the North. Many women hoped for better employment opportunities in the North because, in the South, they faced much competition for domestic employment and men tended to get agricultural work. To aid with this transition, Barrier Williams helped secure job placement in the North for many women before they even began their journey.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9a1231f9-ecfe-45cd-958a-fb4eeba317b6","content":"<p>To introduce and illustrate Barrier Williams&rsquo;s integral role in supporting other Black women as their circumstances changed during part of the Great Migration</p>"},{"id":"8b7fde5f-9fb7-4836-9d75-40f313745d33","content":"<p>To establish that Barrier Williams used her professional connections to arrange employment for other Black women, including jobs with the <em>Chicago Defender</em></p>"},{"id":"e936678b-f1e7-4838-aa45-654285051630","content":"<p>To demonstrate that the factors that motivated the start of the Great Migration were different for Black women than they were for Black men</p>"},{"id":"e2dc5020-ed02-4195-afc9-9aae00c4d661","content":"<p>To provide an overview of the employment challenges faced by Black women in the agricultural and domestic spheres in the southern United States</p>"}],"keys":["9a1231f9-ecfe-45cd-958a-fb4eeba317b6"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes the text&rsquo;s purpose, which is to discuss the important role Barrier Williams played in supporting many other Black women as they relocated to the northern United States during the early years of the Great Migration. After introducing Barrier Williams, the text describes how she helped find jobs for other Black women, who in many cases relocated in search of better employment prospects than the South could offer at the time. The text indicates that by doing so, she eased these women&rsquo;s transition as their circumstances changed. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although the text mentions Barrier Williams&rsquo;s work as a political activist and writer for the <em>Chicago Defender</em>, it doesn&rsquo;t discuss any professional connections she made in these roles or indicate that she used any such connections in her work to secure employment for other Black women. Choice C is incorrect. Although the text discusses a factor that caused many women to relocate during the Great Migration, their difficulty finding employment in the South, the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate that this factor motivated the start of the Great Migration. Moreover, the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss the factors that motivated Black men to migrate. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text mentions the difficult employment prospects for Black women in the domestic and agricultural sectors in the South during the Great Migration, the text&rsquo;s main purpose isn&rsquo;t to provide an overview of the employment challenges Black women faced in these sectors. Rather, it provides this information to show that Barrier Williams played a crucial role in supporting many Black women who relocated to the North by helping them achieve one of their main goals, securing a job. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-051-TSP","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"a5ab3a5a-be7a-4eb1-a287-41cdefdcc610","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959324,"updateDate":1691007959324}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959324, 1691007959324),
    ($SATQ$b35e2fdc$SATQ$, $SATQ$ce55ecd0-6a7f-4cdc-901a-b03c4e6182fd$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>A casual description of Scherezade Garc&iacute;a&rsquo;s 2019 mural <em>Blame It on the Bean: The Power of Coffee</em> can make the work seem <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span>&mdash;a painting that is housed in a coffee shop and that depicts three women drinking coffee may not sound particularly ambitious&mdash;but in fact the work is a complex, dynamic meditation on gender and the legacy of colonialism that demands serious attention. &nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c01625db-a1a7-4cbb-9c23-0343d636a24b","content":"<p>unassuming</p>"},{"id":"4fe1f2f3-4fae-4322-bedc-40992346383f","content":"<p>shrewd</p>"},{"id":"4627b4dc-e897-4fa7-bae6-c4f179c5643d","content":"<p>incongruous</p>"},{"id":"62967af4-bbae-4c18-baa1-5af5b1491a92","content":"<p>pretentious</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c01625db-a1a7-4cbb-9c23-0343d636a24b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Scherezade Garc&iacute;a&rsquo;s mural <em>Blame It on the Bean: The Power of Coffee</em>. In this context, &ldquo;unassuming&rdquo; means ordinary or unremarkable. The text draws a contrast between a &ldquo;casual description&rdquo; of the mural&rsquo;s ordinary location (a coffee shop) and subject matter (three women drinking coffee)&mdash;details that would make it seem relatively unambitious&mdash;and a characterization of the painting as a &ldquo;dynamic meditation&rdquo; on gender and colonialism deserving of &ldquo;serious attention.&rdquo; This context suggests that the mural has significant depth and complexity, but a superficial description of it might make the mural seem ordinary and unremarkable&mdash;that is, unassuming.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;shrewd&rdquo; would mean clever or astute, and there&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that a casual yet misleading description that only mentions the apparent simplicity of the mural&rsquo;s location and subject matter would make the mural seem particularly clever or astute. Though it&rsquo;s possible that the text&rsquo;s assertion that the mural is a &ldquo;complex, dynamic meditation&rdquo; demanding &ldquo;serious attention&rdquo; might convey the idea that it&rsquo;s a particularly clever or astute&mdash;that is, shrewd&mdash;artwork, the text wouldn&rsquo;t suggest that a casual description that fails to account for the work&rsquo;s complexity would likewise characterize the work as shrewd. Choice C is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;incongruous&rdquo; would mean unsuitable for its surroundings or internally inconsistent. The &ldquo;casual description&rdquo; presented in the text indicates that the painting is housed in a coffee shop and depicts women drinking coffee, which would imply that the mural may in fact be well suited to its surroundings, not that it&rsquo;s ill suited to its location. Moreover, none of the details mentioned in this description would suggest that the painting contains internal inconsistencies of any kind. Choice D is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;pretentious&rdquo; would mean expressive of exaggerated importance, which wouldn&rsquo;t fit the contrast established in the text between a &ldquo;casual description&rdquo; of the painting and the work&rsquo;s deeper themes. Though the text argues that the painting is worthy of &ldquo;serious attention,&rdquo; which would suggest its importance, the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that the casual description would by contrast imply that the painting&rsquo;s importance is exaggerated. Rather, by merely mentioning the mural&rsquo;s relatively ordinary location and subject matter without reference to this complexity, the casual description conveys that the painting is more unassuming and understated than it actually is, not that it expresses an exaggerated self-importance.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b35e2fdc","external_id":"ce55ecd0-6a7f-4cdc-901a-b03c4e6182fd","vaultid":null,"uId":"fba2c231-ee28-4835-9a5b-1e48a9c6295b","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>A casual description of Scherezade Garc&iacute;a&rsquo;s 2019 mural <em>Blame It on the Bean: The Power of Coffee</em> can make the work seem <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span>&mdash;a painting that is housed in a coffee shop and that depicts three women drinking coffee may not sound particularly ambitious&mdash;but in fact the work is a complex, dynamic meditation on gender and the legacy of colonialism that demands serious attention. &nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c01625db-a1a7-4cbb-9c23-0343d636a24b","content":"<p>unassuming</p>"},{"id":"4fe1f2f3-4fae-4322-bedc-40992346383f","content":"<p>shrewd</p>"},{"id":"4627b4dc-e897-4fa7-bae6-c4f179c5643d","content":"<p>incongruous</p>"},{"id":"62967af4-bbae-4c18-baa1-5af5b1491a92","content":"<p>pretentious</p>"}],"keys":["c01625db-a1a7-4cbb-9c23-0343d636a24b"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Scherezade Garc&iacute;a&rsquo;s mural <em>Blame It on the Bean: The Power of Coffee</em>. In this context, &ldquo;unassuming&rdquo; means ordinary or unremarkable. The text draws a contrast between a &ldquo;casual description&rdquo; of the mural&rsquo;s ordinary location (a coffee shop) and subject matter (three women drinking coffee)&mdash;details that would make it seem relatively unambitious&mdash;and a characterization of the painting as a &ldquo;dynamic meditation&rdquo; on gender and colonialism deserving of &ldquo;serious attention.&rdquo; This context suggests that the mural has significant depth and complexity, but a superficial description of it might make the mural seem ordinary and unremarkable&mdash;that is, unassuming.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;shrewd&rdquo; would mean clever or astute, and there&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that a casual yet misleading description that only mentions the apparent simplicity of the mural&rsquo;s location and subject matter would make the mural seem particularly clever or astute. Though it&rsquo;s possible that the text&rsquo;s assertion that the mural is a &ldquo;complex, dynamic meditation&rdquo; demanding &ldquo;serious attention&rdquo; might convey the idea that it&rsquo;s a particularly clever or astute&mdash;that is, shrewd&mdash;artwork, the text wouldn&rsquo;t suggest that a casual description that fails to account for the work&rsquo;s complexity would likewise characterize the work as shrewd. Choice C is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;incongruous&rdquo; would mean unsuitable for its surroundings or internally inconsistent. The &ldquo;casual description&rdquo; presented in the text indicates that the painting is housed in a coffee shop and depicts women drinking coffee, which would imply that the mural may in fact be well suited to its surroundings, not that it&rsquo;s ill suited to its location. Moreover, none of the details mentioned in this description would suggest that the painting contains internal inconsistencies of any kind. Choice D is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;pretentious&rdquo; would mean expressive of exaggerated importance, which wouldn&rsquo;t fit the contrast established in the text between a &ldquo;casual description&rdquo; of the painting and the work&rsquo;s deeper themes. Though the text argues that the painting is worthy of &ldquo;serious attention,&rdquo; which would suggest its importance, the text doesn&rsquo;t suggest that the casual description would by contrast imply that the painting&rsquo;s importance is exaggerated. Rather, by merely mentioning the mural&rsquo;s relatively ordinary location and subject matter without reference to this complexity, the casual description conveys that the painting is more unassuming and understated than it actually is, not that it expresses an exaggerated self-importance.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771170,"updateDate":1776362771170}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771170, 1776362771170),
    ($SATQ$b3e145e4$SATQ$, $SATQ$52ed9f78-57e4-49db-8d52-e1b7d3ad5772$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In the 1950s, scientists didn&rsquo;t know much about the ocean floor. <span style="text-decoration: underline;" role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">Many scientists at the time believed that the ocean floor was mostly flat.</span> But geologist Marie Tharp and her research partner, Bruce Heezen, proved that this idea was wrong. Using sonar data collected from the Atlantic Ocean, Tharp and Heezen showed that the floor was filled with canyons, mountains, and valleys.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"7873cf23-4c10-48ec-84d0-ccd56f32803e","content":"<p>It identifies a scientific belief that Tharp and Heezen showed to be wrong.</p>"},{"id":"b737d93d-913e-4001-b347-f91bdfdcf000","content":"<p>It describes the design of Tharp and Heezen&rsquo;s experiment.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"5c8d09fd-f7ca-4247-861b-ace3b6f072f4","content":"<p>It emphasizes a disagreement between Tharp and Heezen.</p>"},{"id":"9aafd7ad-7ca3-4b13-8319-c4a74b03fb15","content":"<p>It presents data to support a claim that Tharp and Heezen made.&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["7873cf23-4c10-48ec-84d0-ccd56f32803e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes how the underlined sentence functions in the text as a whole. The first sentence of the text establishes that scientists didn&rsquo;t know much about the ocean floor in the 1950s. The second sentence, which is underlined, describes what many scientists thought at the time&mdash;that the ocean floor was mostly flat. The remainder of the text establishes that the ocean floor is far from flat, citing research conducted by Marie Tharp and Bruce Heezen. Thus, the purpose of the underlined sentence is to identify a scientific belief that Tharp and Heezen showed to be wrong.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although Tharp and Heezen&rsquo;s work with sonar data in the Atlantic Ocean is mentioned later in the text, the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t describe the design of their experiment. Instead, it identifies a belief held by scientists that Tharp and Heezen demonstrated to be wrong. Choice C is incorrect because the underlined sentence presents a belief held by many scientists in the 1950s; nowhere does the text mention a disagreement between Tharp and Heezen, whom the text describes as research partners working together to map the ocean floor. Choice D is incorrect because the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t present data in support of a claim; instead, it presents a scientific belief that Tharp and Heezen&rsquo;s work showed to be wrong.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b3e145e4","external_id":"52ed9f78-57e4-49db-8d52-e1b7d3ad5772","vaultid":null,"uId":"aad1548f-6e40-4882-bee8-7c87df1ee4af","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In the 1950s, scientists didn&rsquo;t know much about the ocean floor. <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">Many scientists at the time believed that the ocean floor was mostly flat.</span> But geologist Marie Tharp and her research partner, Bruce Heezen, proved that this idea was wrong. Using sonar data collected from the Atlantic Ocean, Tharp and Heezen showed that the floor was filled with canyons, mountains, and valleys.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"7873cf23-4c10-48ec-84d0-ccd56f32803e","content":"<p>It identifies a scientific belief that Tharp and Heezen showed to be wrong.</p>"},{"id":"b737d93d-913e-4001-b347-f91bdfdcf000","content":"<p>It describes the design of Tharp and Heezen&rsquo;s experiment.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"5c8d09fd-f7ca-4247-861b-ace3b6f072f4","content":"<p>It emphasizes a disagreement between Tharp and Heezen.</p>"},{"id":"9aafd7ad-7ca3-4b13-8319-c4a74b03fb15","content":"<p>It presents data to support a claim that Tharp and Heezen made.&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["7873cf23-4c10-48ec-84d0-ccd56f32803e"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes how the underlined sentence functions in the text as a whole. The first sentence of the text establishes that scientists didn&rsquo;t know much about the ocean floor in the 1950s. The second sentence, which is underlined, describes what many scientists thought at the time&mdash;that the ocean floor was mostly flat. The remainder of the text establishes that the ocean floor is far from flat, citing research conducted by Marie Tharp and Bruce Heezen. Thus, the purpose of the underlined sentence is to identify a scientific belief that Tharp and Heezen showed to be wrong.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although Tharp and Heezen&rsquo;s work with sonar data in the Atlantic Ocean is mentioned later in the text, the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t describe the design of their experiment. Instead, it identifies a belief held by scientists that Tharp and Heezen demonstrated to be wrong. Choice C is incorrect because the underlined sentence presents a belief held by many scientists in the 1950s; nowhere does the text mention a disagreement between Tharp and Heezen, whom the text describes as research partners working together to map the ocean floor. Choice D is incorrect because the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t present data in support of a claim; instead, it presents a scientific belief that Tharp and Heezen&rsquo;s work showed to be wrong.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669207,"updateDate":1743430669207}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669207, 1743430669207),
    ($SATQ$b411eb09$SATQ$, $SATQ$22aee311-bf13-42f1-867e-fbf71ee4ecfd$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$1c10a1fb-8270-497d-bbae-ad8a4e790ba0$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>New and interesting research conducted by Suleiman A. Al-Sweedan and Moath Alhaj is inspired by their observation that though there have been many studies of the effect of high altitude on blood chemistry, there is a <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level, such as the California towns of Salton City and Seeley.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2883e722-8b00-47c1-a26c-31474f6f1648","content":"<p>quarrel about</p>"},{"id":"3a413c85-3069-46dd-9dde-7f37e20ee26f","content":"<p>paucity of</p>"},{"id":"8b8b9f4b-8313-497f-abe0-325f7347b9e8","content":"<p>profusion of</p>"},{"id":"e33d710f-c13d-4fb0-ad7b-aef1cb170507","content":"<p>verisimilitude in</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3a413c85-3069-46dd-9dde-7f37e20ee26f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically and precisely completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of studies of altitude&rsquo;s effect on blood chemistry. In this context, &ldquo;paucity of&rdquo; means lack of. In describing the inspiration behind Al-Sweedan and Alhaj&rsquo;s research, the text uses the word &ldquo;though&rdquo; to suggest a contrasting relationship between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. This contrasting relationship and the text&rsquo;s use of the word &ldquo;many&rdquo; provide context suggesting that there are few, if any, examples of the second type of study, whereas there are numerous examples of the first type. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context for there to be a &ldquo;quarrel about,&rdquo; or open disagreement about, studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. The text&rsquo;s use of the words &ldquo;though&rdquo; and &ldquo;many&rdquo; suggests a contrasting relationship in terms of amount between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. There&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that the contrast between the two types of studies involves the extent to which researchers broadly agree or disagree about the contents of either type. Choice C is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context for there to be a &ldquo;profusion of,&rdquo; or great abundance of, studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. The text&rsquo;s use of the words &ldquo;though&rdquo; and &ldquo;many&rdquo; suggests a contrasting relationship in terms of amount between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. Rather than logically completing this contrast, &ldquo;profusion of&rdquo; would indicate that the two types of studies are similar in terms of amount, with many examples existing of both types. Choice D is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context for there to be a &ldquo;verisimilitude in,&rdquo; or appearance of truth in, studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. The text&rsquo;s use of the words &ldquo;though&rdquo; and &ldquo;many&rdquo; suggests a contrasting relationship in terms of amount between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. There&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that the contrast between the two types of studies involves the extent to which either type of study presents an appearance of truth. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$T2013$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$4cd66247-291b-48e7-9f2b-8732d7b8204b$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$25$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b411eb09","external_id":"22aee311-bf13-42f1-867e-fbf71ee4ecfd","vaultid":"1c10a1fb-8270-497d-bbae-ad8a4e790ba0","uId":"74d8972a-1c58-45c2-b6dc-e4942de18ff6","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>New and interesting research conducted by Suleiman A. Al-Sweedan and Moath Alhaj is inspired by their observation that though there have been many studies of the effect of high altitude on blood chemistry, there is a <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level, such as the California towns of Salton City and Seeley.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2883e722-8b00-47c1-a26c-31474f6f1648","content":"<p>quarrel about</p>"},{"id":"3a413c85-3069-46dd-9dde-7f37e20ee26f","content":"<p>paucity of</p>"},{"id":"8b8b9f4b-8313-497f-abe0-325f7347b9e8","content":"<p>profusion of</p>"},{"id":"e33d710f-c13d-4fb0-ad7b-aef1cb170507","content":"<p>verisimilitude in</p>"}],"keys":["3a413c85-3069-46dd-9dde-7f37e20ee26f"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically and precisely completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of studies of altitude&rsquo;s effect on blood chemistry. In this context, &ldquo;paucity of&rdquo; means lack of. In describing the inspiration behind Al-Sweedan and Alhaj&rsquo;s research, the text uses the word &ldquo;though&rdquo; to suggest a contrasting relationship between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. This contrasting relationship and the text&rsquo;s use of the word &ldquo;many&rdquo; provide context suggesting that there are few, if any, examples of the second type of study, whereas there are numerous examples of the first type. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context for there to be a &ldquo;quarrel about,&rdquo; or open disagreement about, studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. The text&rsquo;s use of the words &ldquo;though&rdquo; and &ldquo;many&rdquo; suggests a contrasting relationship in terms of amount between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. There&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that the contrast between the two types of studies involves the extent to which researchers broadly agree or disagree about the contents of either type. Choice C is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context for there to be a &ldquo;profusion of,&rdquo; or great abundance of, studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. The text&rsquo;s use of the words &ldquo;though&rdquo; and &ldquo;many&rdquo; suggests a contrasting relationship in terms of amount between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. Rather than logically completing this contrast, &ldquo;profusion of&rdquo; would indicate that the two types of studies are similar in terms of amount, with many examples existing of both types. Choice D is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context for there to be a &ldquo;verisimilitude in,&rdquo; or appearance of truth in, studies of the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. The text&rsquo;s use of the words &ldquo;though&rdquo; and &ldquo;many&rdquo; suggests a contrasting relationship in terms of amount between two types of studies: those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living at a high altitude and those examining the effect on blood chemistry of living in locations below sea level. There&rsquo;s nothing in the text to suggest that the contrast between the two types of studies involves the extent to which either type of study presents an appearance of truth. </p>","parenttemplatename":"T2013","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"4cd66247-291b-48e7-9f2b-8732d7b8204b","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"25","createDate":1691007959378,"updateDate":1691007959378}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959378, 1691007959378),
    ($SATQ$b44066dc$SATQ$, $SATQ$474df432-dad4-409f-9668-6060c937748a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Economist Jingting Fan argues that the effects of international trade may display spatial variation at sub-national levels. For instance, imported goods may reduce expenses for a country&rsquo;s average consumer, but for consumers living far from ports, high intranational transport costs could <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> the price advantages associated with imports.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9538adf8-2b44-4b18-91e6-2b20bf1d44cf","content":"<p>nullify</p>"},{"id":"0518f569-d700-4fa1-928e-a56740042306","content":"<p>denigrate</p>"},{"id":"7bd98790-9f37-4bce-b0c8-b802ac25d708","content":"<p>underestimate</p>"},{"id":"b5666fa6-51ed-4487-9927-00d4bedbb704","content":"<p>misconstrue</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9538adf8-2b44-4b18-91e6-2b20bf1d44cf"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of imported goods and consumer prices. In this context, "nullify" most nearly means negate or undermine. The text indicates that importing goods to a country can reduce consumer prices in that country, then cautions that the costs of transporting goods within the country is also a factor. These transportation costs likely raise the prices that must be paid by people who live far from the ports of entry. Therefore, the intranational transportation costs could nullify the price advantages to consumers of importing goods.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. In this context, "denigrate" would most nearly mean disparage or deny the importance of. Since transportation costs would not be capable of denying the importance of price advantages, it would not make sense to state that intranational transportation costs denigrate the price advantages of importing goods. Choice C is incorrect. In this context, "underestimate" would most nearly mean predict a lower value for, or to undervalue, someone or something. Though transportation costs might be undervalued, they cannot themselves undervalue something else, so it would not make sense to state that intranational transportation costs underestimate the price advantages of importing goods. Choice D is incorrect. In this context, "misconstrue" would most nearly mean misunderstand. Since transport costs are not capable of understanding, it would not make sense to claim that intranational transportation costs misconstrue the price advantages of importing goods.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b44066dc","external_id":"474df432-dad4-409f-9668-6060c937748a","vaultid":null,"uId":"605dec6f-f313-4cdd-83a4-1461e9581d1a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Economist Jingting Fan argues that the effects of international trade may display spatial variation at sub-national levels. For instance, imported goods may reduce expenses for a country&rsquo;s average consumer, but for consumers living far from ports, high intranational transport costs could <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> the price advantages associated with imports.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9538adf8-2b44-4b18-91e6-2b20bf1d44cf","content":"<p>nullify</p>"},{"id":"0518f569-d700-4fa1-928e-a56740042306","content":"<p>denigrate</p>"},{"id":"7bd98790-9f37-4bce-b0c8-b802ac25d708","content":"<p>underestimate</p>"},{"id":"b5666fa6-51ed-4487-9927-00d4bedbb704","content":"<p>misconstrue</p>"}],"keys":["9538adf8-2b44-4b18-91e6-2b20bf1d44cf"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of imported goods and consumer prices. In this context, \"nullify\" most nearly means negate or undermine. The text indicates that importing goods to a country can reduce consumer prices in that country, then cautions that the costs of transporting goods within the country is also a factor. These transportation costs likely raise the prices that must be paid by people who live far from the ports of entry. Therefore, the intranational transportation costs could nullify the price advantages to consumers of importing goods.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. In this context, \"denigrate\" would most nearly mean disparage or deny the importance of. Since transportation costs would not be capable of denying the importance of price advantages, it would not make sense to state that intranational transportation costs denigrate the price advantages of importing goods. Choice C is incorrect. In this context, \"underestimate\" would most nearly mean predict a lower value for, or to undervalue, someone or something. Though transportation costs might be undervalued, they cannot themselves undervalue something else, so it would not make sense to state that intranational transportation costs underestimate the price advantages of importing goods. Choice D is incorrect. In this context, \"misconstrue\" would most nearly mean misunderstand. Since transport costs are not capable of understanding, it would not make sense to claim that intranational transportation costs misconstrue the price advantages of importing goods.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323052,"updateDate":1730147323052}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323052, 1730147323052),
    ($SATQ$b4887dae$SATQ$, $SATQ$cfed6bf7-ec1f-4dd1-bc04-daa74a4bb1a3$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$154647ff-d608-4cb8-b1f4-389bfa5ec640$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Mathematician Claude Shannon is widely regarded as a foundational figure in information theory. His most important paper, &ldquo;A Mathematical Theory of Communication,&rdquo; published in 1948 when he was employed at Bell Labs, utilized a concept called a &ldquo;binary digit&rdquo; (shortened to &ldquo;bit&rdquo;) to measure the amount of information in any signal and determine the fastest rate at which information could be transmitted while still being reliably decipherable. Robert Gallagher, one of Shannon&rsquo;s colleagues, said that the bit was &ldquo;[Shannon&rsquo;s] discovery, and from it the whole communications revolution has sprung.&rdquo;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3793af1f-e158-4f4f-874d-a5f39fef6e8f","content":"<p>It presents a theoretical concept, illustrates how the name of the concept has changed, and shows how the name has entered common usage.</p>"},{"id":"a6800f98-e09d-412a-af97-4eef83b904c7","content":"<p>It introduces a respected researcher, describes an aspect of his work, and suggests why the work is historically significant.</p>"},{"id":"a42ae42a-8016-46cb-9340-33706b4b8e18","content":"<p>It names the company where an important mathematician worked, details the mathematician&rsquo;s career at the company, and provides an example of the recognition he received there.</p>"},{"id":"a1f6280d-5a53-4873-aeb5-3999101f569d","content":"<p>It mentions a paper, offers a summary of the paper&rsquo;s findings, and presents a researcher&rsquo;s commentary on the paper.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a6800f98-e09d-412a-af97-4eef83b904c7"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text starts with a general statement that introduces Shannon, then describes a specific contribution from one of his papers, then provides a quote that illustrates just how important this contribution was. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text only mentions very briefly, in parentheses, that &ldquo;binary digit&rdquo; was shortened to &ldquo;bit.&rdquo; It doesn&rsquo;t go into detail about this name change, and it doesn&rsquo;t discuss any &ldquo;common usage&rdquo; of the name at all. Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. Shannon&rsquo;s employment at Bell Labs is only mentioned once, very briefly: the text never goes into detail about his career there, and it never mentions any recognition he received there. Choice D is incorrect. This is too narrow. Overall, the text is about Shannon&rsquo;s importance in his field, not just this one paper of his. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TSP-H004$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$abe64155-ae37-4267-9d6c-3ce41faeef99$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b4887dae","external_id":"cfed6bf7-ec1f-4dd1-bc04-daa74a4bb1a3","vaultid":"154647ff-d608-4cb8-b1f4-389bfa5ec640","uId":"56b1bb4c-306d-49a9-bc32-3cf03a66363e","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Mathematician Claude Shannon is widely regarded as a foundational figure in information theory. His most important paper, &ldquo;A Mathematical Theory of Communication,&rdquo; published in 1948 when he was employed at Bell Labs, utilized a concept called a &ldquo;binary digit&rdquo; (shortened to &ldquo;bit&rdquo;) to measure the amount of information in any signal and determine the fastest rate at which information could be transmitted while still being reliably decipherable. Robert Gallagher, one of Shannon&rsquo;s colleagues, said that the bit was &ldquo;[Shannon&rsquo;s] discovery, and from it the whole communications revolution has sprung.&rdquo;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3793af1f-e158-4f4f-874d-a5f39fef6e8f","content":"<p>It presents a theoretical concept, illustrates how the name of the concept has changed, and shows how the name has entered common usage.</p>"},{"id":"a6800f98-e09d-412a-af97-4eef83b904c7","content":"<p>It introduces a respected researcher, describes an aspect of his work, and suggests why the work is historically significant.</p>"},{"id":"a42ae42a-8016-46cb-9340-33706b4b8e18","content":"<p>It names the company where an important mathematician worked, details the mathematician&rsquo;s career at the company, and provides an example of the recognition he received there.</p>"},{"id":"a1f6280d-5a53-4873-aeb5-3999101f569d","content":"<p>It mentions a paper, offers a summary of the paper&rsquo;s findings, and presents a researcher&rsquo;s commentary on the paper.</p>"}],"keys":["a6800f98-e09d-412a-af97-4eef83b904c7"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text starts with a general statement that introduces Shannon, then describes a specific contribution from one of his papers, then provides a quote that illustrates just how important this contribution was. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text only mentions very briefly, in parentheses, that &ldquo;binary digit&rdquo; was shortened to &ldquo;bit.&rdquo; It doesn&rsquo;t go into detail about this name change, and it doesn&rsquo;t discuss any &ldquo;common usage&rdquo; of the name at all. Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. Shannon&rsquo;s employment at Bell Labs is only mentioned once, very briefly: the text never goes into detail about his career there, and it never mentions any recognition he received there. Choice D is incorrect. This is too narrow. Overall, the text is about Shannon&rsquo;s importance in his field, not just this one paper of his. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TSP-H004","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"abe64155-ae37-4267-9d6c-3ce41faeef99","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959375,"updateDate":1691007959375}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959375, 1691007959375),
    ($SATQ$b4c6cff6$SATQ$, $SATQ$4903c40b-ba93-4f98-9f88-9eb2761045ec$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$90402771-565e-482f-a35a-477762c6b4a1$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is adapted from Karel Čapek&rsquo;s 1920 play <em>R.U.R. (Rossum&rsquo;s Universal Robots</em>), translated by Paul Selver and Nigel Playfair in 1923. Fabry and Busman are telling Miss Glory why their company manufactures robots.</p>
<p style="padding-left:1em">FABRY: One Robot can replace two and a half&nbsp;<em>workmen</em>. The human machine, Miss Glory, was terribly&nbsp;<em>imperfect</em>. It had to be removed sooner or later.</p>
<p style="padding-left:1em">BUSMAN: It was too expensive.</p>
<p style="padding-left:1em">FABRY: It was not <em>effective</em>. It no longer <span role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content"><u>answers</u></span> the requirements of&nbsp;<em>modern engineering</em>. Nature has no idea of keeping pace with&nbsp;<em>modern labor</em>.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;answers&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"febedb21-15a1-4eb2-a3b4-5c8aa1d611b5","content":"<p>Explains</p>"},{"id":"6c560069-7c1d-439f-ada4-1e16df138226","content":"<p>Rebuts</p>"},{"id":"8b0175cf-1a52-4db2-9c57-3e0c6311669a","content":"<p>Defends</p>"},{"id":"a43baabd-93df-439d-97c5-d82a1a5f13a8","content":"<p>Fulfills</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a43baabd-93df-439d-97c5-d82a1a5f13a8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because as used in the text, &ldquo;answers&rdquo; most nearly means fulfills. In the text, Fabry and Busman claim that the robots manufactured by their company are more efficient than human workers, which they refer to as &ldquo;the human machine.&rdquo; Fabry observes that the human machine &ldquo;no longer answers the requirements of <em>modern engineering</em>.&rdquo; That is, human workers are incapable of meeting the rigorous needs of modern, industrialized workplaces. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although in some contexts &ldquo;answers&rdquo; can mean explains, it doesn&rsquo;t have that meaning in this context because the topic under discussion is human beings&rsquo; inability to perform labor efficiently, not their inability to engage in discussion or explanation.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect. Although in some contexts &ldquo;answers&rdquo; can mean rebuts, or proves a claim or argument to be false, it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to speak of proving<em> </em>requirements<em> </em>to be false; requirements might or might not be reasonable, but they can&rsquo;t be verified as truthful or untruthful, as claims or accusations can.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. Although in some contexts, &ldquo;answers&rdquo; can mean defends against criticism, or justifies, it doesn&rsquo;t have that meaning in this context because the opinion that Fabry expresses is that human workers can no longer fulfill the requirements of modern workplaces, not that they have ceased to justify those requirements or to defend them against criticism; indeed, there is no suggestion in the text that workers ever defended those requirements.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-033-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$dff50a65-b58b-4970-9a3d-0c58bae2d59a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b4c6cff6","external_id":"4903c40b-ba93-4f98-9f88-9eb2761045ec","vaultid":"90402771-565e-482f-a35a-477762c6b4a1","uId":"bf4d194d-8fb1-49d6-83cf-0ff34ffbd53a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is adapted from Karel Čapek&rsquo;s 1920 play <em>R.U.R. (Rossum&rsquo;s Universal Robots</em>), translated by Paul Selver and Nigel Playfair in 1923. Fabry and Busman are telling Miss Glory why their company manufactures robots.</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:1em\">FABRY: One Robot can replace two and a half&nbsp;<em>workmen</em>. The human machine, Miss Glory, was terribly&nbsp;<em>imperfect</em>. It had to be removed sooner or later.</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:1em\">BUSMAN: It was too expensive.</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left:1em\">FABRY: It was not <em>effective</em>. It no longer <span role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\"><u>answers</u></span> the requirements of&nbsp;<em>modern engineering</em>. Nature has no idea of keeping pace with&nbsp;<em>modern labor</em>.&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;answers&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"febedb21-15a1-4eb2-a3b4-5c8aa1d611b5","content":"<p>Explains</p>"},{"id":"6c560069-7c1d-439f-ada4-1e16df138226","content":"<p>Rebuts</p>"},{"id":"8b0175cf-1a52-4db2-9c57-3e0c6311669a","content":"<p>Defends</p>"},{"id":"a43baabd-93df-439d-97c5-d82a1a5f13a8","content":"<p>Fulfills</p>"}],"keys":["a43baabd-93df-439d-97c5-d82a1a5f13a8"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because as used in the text, &ldquo;answers&rdquo; most nearly means fulfills. In the text, Fabry and Busman claim that the robots manufactured by their company are more efficient than human workers, which they refer to as &ldquo;the human machine.&rdquo; Fabry observes that the human machine &ldquo;no longer answers the requirements of <em>modern engineering</em>.&rdquo; That is, human workers are incapable of meeting the rigorous needs of modern, industrialized workplaces. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although in some contexts &ldquo;answers&rdquo; can mean explains, it doesn&rsquo;t have that meaning in this context because the topic under discussion is human beings&rsquo; inability to perform labor efficiently, not their inability to engage in discussion or explanation.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect. Although in some contexts &ldquo;answers&rdquo; can mean rebuts, or proves a claim or argument to be false, it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to speak of proving<em> </em>requirements<em> </em>to be false; requirements might or might not be reasonable, but they can&rsquo;t be verified as truthful or untruthful, as claims or accusations can.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. Although in some contexts, &ldquo;answers&rdquo; can mean defends against criticism, or justifies, it doesn&rsquo;t have that meaning in this context because the opinion that Fabry expresses is that human workers can no longer fulfill the requirements of modern workplaces, not that they have ceased to justify those requirements or to defend them against criticism; indeed, there is no suggestion in the text that workers ever defended those requirements.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-033-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"dff50a65-b58b-4970-9a3d-0c58bae2d59a","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959319,"updateDate":1691007959319}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959319, 1691007959319),
    ($SATQ$b4d29611$SATQ$, $SATQ$317acb11-f400-4eba-8a07-a4f9f2389131$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$6157f44f-0cec-41a7-bb58-af0558f52a1d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Michelene Pesantubbee, a historian and citizen of the Choctaw Nation, has identified a dilemma inherent to research on the status of women in her tribe during the 1600s and 1700s: the primary sources from that era, travel narratives and other accounts by male European colonizers, underestimate the degree of power conferred on Choctaw women by their traditional roles in political, civic, and ceremonial life. Pesantubbee argues that the Choctaw oral tradition and findings from archaeological sites in the tribe&rsquo;s homeland supplement the written record by providing crucial insights into those roles.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f88c54d5-9036-4923-bb81-85b665df9af4","content":"<p>It details the shortcomings of certain historical sources, then argues that research should avoid those sources altogether.</p>"},{"id":"d934f5db-a98e-45b7-862b-195ed0f0cb59","content":"<p>It describes a problem that arises in research on a particular topic, then sketches a historian&rsquo;s approach to addressing that problem.</p>"},{"id":"4e51181c-a1d3-470b-b8b9-1d752cd69c38","content":"<p>It lists the advantages of a particular research method, then acknowledges a historian&rsquo;s criticism of that method.</p>"},{"id":"c9649b56-fbfd-42f5-a7c1-5a1fbb3af5fe","content":"<p>It characterizes a particular topic as especially challenging to research, then suggests a related topic for historians to pursue instead.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d934f5db-a98e-45b7-862b-195ed0f0cb59"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text begins by stating a problem with research on the status of Choctaw women in the 1600s and 1700s: written primary sources underestimate the power they had in their traditional roles. Then it presents one historian&rsquo;s solution: looking to oral tradition and archeological findings for more insight into these roles. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text never says that research should avoid written primary sources, just that research should also use oral tradition and archeological sites as sources. Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text never mentions the advantages of using written primary sources. Choice D is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text never says that the status of Choctaw women during the 1600s and 1700s is too challenging to research. And it doesn&rsquo;t mention any other topics to research instead. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TSP-M003$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$37f4ff0e-73e8-46be-9ca3-08b2d3aa7d43$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b4d29611","external_id":"317acb11-f400-4eba-8a07-a4f9f2389131","vaultid":"6157f44f-0cec-41a7-bb58-af0558f52a1d","uId":"e92aaa3a-7c96-442b-9dff-e9d2bf7aff7d","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Michelene Pesantubbee, a historian and citizen of the Choctaw Nation, has identified a dilemma inherent to research on the status of women in her tribe during the 1600s and 1700s: the primary sources from that era, travel narratives and other accounts by male European colonizers, underestimate the degree of power conferred on Choctaw women by their traditional roles in political, civic, and ceremonial life. Pesantubbee argues that the Choctaw oral tradition and findings from archaeological sites in the tribe&rsquo;s homeland supplement the written record by providing crucial insights into those roles.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f88c54d5-9036-4923-bb81-85b665df9af4","content":"<p>It details the shortcomings of certain historical sources, then argues that research should avoid those sources altogether.</p>"},{"id":"d934f5db-a98e-45b7-862b-195ed0f0cb59","content":"<p>It describes a problem that arises in research on a particular topic, then sketches a historian&rsquo;s approach to addressing that problem.</p>"},{"id":"4e51181c-a1d3-470b-b8b9-1d752cd69c38","content":"<p>It lists the advantages of a particular research method, then acknowledges a historian&rsquo;s criticism of that method.</p>"},{"id":"c9649b56-fbfd-42f5-a7c1-5a1fbb3af5fe","content":"<p>It characterizes a particular topic as especially challenging to research, then suggests a related topic for historians to pursue instead.</p>"}],"keys":["d934f5db-a98e-45b7-862b-195ed0f0cb59"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text begins by stating a problem with research on the status of Choctaw women in the 1600s and 1700s: written primary sources underestimate the power they had in their traditional roles. Then it presents one historian&rsquo;s solution: looking to oral tradition and archeological findings for more insight into these roles. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text never says that research should avoid written primary sources, just that research should also use oral tradition and archeological sites as sources. Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text never mentions the advantages of using written primary sources. Choice D is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the overall structure. The text never says that the status of Choctaw women during the 1600s and 1700s is too challenging to research. And it doesn&rsquo;t mention any other topics to research instead. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TSP-M003","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"37f4ff0e-73e8-46be-9ca3-08b2d3aa7d43","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959375,"updateDate":1691007959375}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959375, 1691007959375)
